window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b298-c60db6dcd8237da9.json"]={sha256:"c60db6dcd8237da9bcbf808293557bc752ec9835ba4c4eb202b18accea4aa2e6",value:{"id":"b298","title":"地下水屏障防止海水入侵","titleEn":"Groundwater barriers against seawater intrusion","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以洛杉磯與橘郡海水屏障為背景，逐步區分壓力防護、淡鹹水混合與物質旅行時間。十個原創單元從尖銳界面近似、等效淡水水頭和達西流，深入徑向注入、線性疊加、注入能力與潮汐反應，所有算例均明列理想條件，並用分層觀測檢查解釋是否成立。","summaryEn":"Using Los Angeles and Orange County barriers as context, distinguish hydraulic protection, fresh-saline mixing and material travel time. Ten original units progress from ideal interfaces and equivalent heads through radial injection, superposition, injectivity and tidal response, stating model assumptions and checking interpretations against depth-resolved observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-ecology","architectureNodes":[["密度與壓力基準","Density and pressure datum"],["補注與水頭隆起","Recharge and head buildup"],["分層流動與混合","Layered flow and mixing"],["監測與潮汐辨識","Monitoring and tidal diagnosis"],["成效與不確定度","Performance and uncertainty"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-ecology","labels":["密度與壓力基準","補注與水頭隆起","分層流動與混合","監測與潮汐辨識","成效與不確定度"],"labelsEn":["Density and pressure datum","Recharge and head buildup","Layered flow and mixing","Monitoring and tidal diagnosis","Performance and uncertainty"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"教學假設淡水與鹹水密度分別1000與1025 kg/m³，靜水尖銳界面模型將海面以上0.80 m水頭換算為海面以下32 m界面深度。這不是觀測到的鹽水前緣。另一個獨立算例把100 m路徑除以0.20 m/day孔隙速度，得到500日平流時間；同距離若水力擴散率100000 m²/day，特徵壓力尺度僅0.10日。兩者不能互換，快速水位反應不證明補注水已抵達。請改變密度差與儲水係數，分別重算各自影響的模型，並列出能否證實壓力、混合或水質改善的獨立觀測。","textEn":"Assume fresh and saline densities of 1000 and 1025 kg/m³. An ideal hydrostatic sharp interface converts 0.80 m freshwater elevation above sea level into 32 m interface depth below it; this is not an observed salt front. In a separate calculation, a 100 m path and 0.20 m/day pore velocity imply 500 days of advective travel. Hydraulic diffusivity of 100000 m²/day gives a characteristic pressure scale of only 0.10 day at the same distance. These quantities are not interchangeable, and rapid head response does not prove recharge-water arrival. Vary density contrast and storativity separately, then identify independent evidence for pressure, mixing and quality improvement.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b298-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「密度差與理想淡鹹水界面」與「等效淡水水頭與壓力基準」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface\" and \"Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b298-v15-01","title":"密度差與理想淡鹹水界面：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「密度差與理想淡鹹水界面」如何影響地下水屏障防止海水入侵的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Groundwater barriers against seawater intrusion”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"淡地下水與海水密度不同，在理想靜水平衡下會形成淡水位高出海面的高度與界面深度之間的關係。這個尖銳界面模型把混合帶壓縮成一條線，並忽略地下水流動、分層和抽水引起的局部上升，因此適合理解密度效應，不能直接定位現地鹽水前緣。地下水屏障利用補注改變水頭與流向，不是一道實體不透水牆。實際評估需要同時觀察不同深度的壓力、鹽度和時間變化，不能只在單一水井量到高水位就認定所有含水層已受到保護。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「密度差與理想淡鹹水界面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Fresh groundwater and seawater have different densities. Ideal hydrostatic equilibrium relates freshwater elevation above sea level to interface depth below it. The sharp-interface approximation compresses a mixing zone into a line and omits flow, layering and local pumping-induced upconing, making it useful for understanding density effects rather than locating a field salt front. Recharge barriers alter heads and flow paths rather than forming impermeable walls. Assess pressure, salinity and temporal behavior at multiple depths instead of inferring protection from one high well level. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設靜水、均質非受壓含水層及尖銳界面，淡水密度1000、鹹水1025 kg/m³，淡水位高出海面0.80 m；z=1000×0.80/(1025−1000)=32 m，為海面以下的理想界面深度。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume hydrostatic equilibrium, a homogeneous unconfined aquifer and sharp interface, with densities 1000 and 1025 kg/m³ and freshwater head 0.80 m above sea level.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何海岸含水層只要水位高出海面一公尺，實際鹽水界面就必定精確位於四十公尺深。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every coastal aquifer with one metre of freshwater head has an actual interface exactly forty metres deep.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「密度差與理想淡鹹水界面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-01-k1","title":"密度差與理想淡鹹水界面","titleEn":"Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface","text":"淡地下水與海水密度不同，在理想靜水平衡下會形成淡水位高出海面的高度與界面深度之間的關係。這個尖銳界面模型把混合帶壓縮成一條線，並忽略地下水流動、分層和抽水引起的局部上升，因此適合理解密度效應，不能直接定位現地鹽水前緣。","textEn":"Fresh groundwater and seawater have different densities. Ideal hydrostatic equilibrium relates freshwater elevation above sea level to interface depth below it.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何海岸含水層只要水位高出海面一公尺，實際鹽水界面就必定精確位於四十公尺深。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every coastal aquifer with one metre of freshwater head has an actual interface exactly forty metres deep. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「密度差與理想淡鹹水界面」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface\" is correct?","options":["任何海岸含水層只要水位高出海面一公尺，實際鹽水界面就必定精確位於四十公尺深。","淡地下水與海水密度不同，在理想靜水平衡下會形成淡水位高出海面的高度與界面深度之間的關係。","只要兩口井的水面高程相同，不論井內水的密度如何，壓力狀態就完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Every coastal aquifer with one metre of freshwater head has an actual interface exactly forty metres deep.","Fresh groundwater and seawater have different densities.","Equal water-surface elevations imply identical pressure conditions regardless of fluid density."],"answer":1,"explanation":"淡地下水與海水密度不同，在理想靜水平衡下會形成淡水位高出海面的高度與界面深度之間的關係。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Fresh groundwater and seawater have different densities. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b298-v15-02","title":"密度差與理想淡鹹水界面：定量估算","titleEn":"Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「密度差與理想淡鹹水界面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設靜水、均質非受壓含水層及尖銳界面，淡水密度1000、鹹水1025 kg/m³，淡水位高出海面0.80 m；z=1000×0.80/(1025−1000)=32 m，為海面以下的理想界面深度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume hydrostatic equilibrium, a homogeneous unconfined aquifer and sharp interface, with densities 1000 and 1025 kg/m³ and freshwater head 0.80 m above sea level. Interface depth below sea level is 32 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先以相同海面基準畫出兩側壓力柱，確認界面兩側壓力相等，再檢查密度和深度單位。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw pressure columns using one sea-level datum and verify pressure continuity before checking density and depth units.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設靜水、均質非受壓含水層及尖銳界面，淡水密度1000、鹹水1025 kg/m³，淡水位高出海面0.80 m；z=1000×0.80/(1025−1000)=32 m，為海面以下的理想界面深度。","textEn":"Assume hydrostatic equilibrium, a homogeneous unconfined aquifer and sharp interface, with densities 1000 and 1025 kg/m³ and freshwater head 0.80 m above sea level. Interface depth below sea level is 32 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「密度差與理想淡鹹水界面」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface\", which statement holds?","options":["注入井內壓力升高多少，周圍所有觀測井的含水層水頭就必然同步升高多少。","只要樣本氯離子升高，就能單獨證明海水入侵，且不需要檢查其他來源。","教學假設靜水、均質非受壓含水層及尖銳界面，淡水密度1000、鹹水1025 kg/m³，淡水位高出海面0.80 m。"],"optionsEn":["An injection-well pressure increase must appear unchanged at every surrounding observation well.","An increase in chloride alone proves seawater intrusion without checking any alternative source.","Assume hydrostatic equilibrium, a homogeneous unconfined aquifer and sharp interface, with densities 1000 and 1025 kg/m³ and freshwater head 0.80 m above sea level."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設靜水、均質非受壓含水層及尖銳界面，淡水密度1000、鹹水1025 kg/m³，淡水位高出海面0.80 m；z=1000×0.80/(1025−1000)=32 m，為海面以下的理想界面深度。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume hydrostatic equilibrium, a homogeneous unconfined aquifer and sharp interface, with densities 1000 and 1025 kg/m³ and freshwater head 0.80 m above sea level. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b298-v15-03","title":"密度差與理想淡鹹水界面：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「密度差與理想淡鹹水界面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先以相同海面基準畫出兩側壓力柱，確認界面兩側壓力相等，再檢查密度和深度單位。比較分層鹽度剖面時，記錄混合帶厚度及採樣深度，將理想界面與實測過渡區分開呈現，不把一條計算線包裝成精確地質邊界。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw pressure columns using one sea-level datum and verify pressure continuity before checking density and depth units. Compare depth-resolved salinity observations, recording mixing-zone thickness and sampling depth, and distinguish the ideal interface from the observed transition zone rather than presenting a calculated line as an exact geological boundary. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持淡水位不變，將鹹水密度改為1020 kg/m³並重算深度，再畫出有厚混合帶的剖面。說明哪個結果只是尖銳界面模型的預測，另列出需要補充的壓力與鹽度量測，避免把簡式直接當作場址設計。","observationEn":"Site practice: Hold freshwater head fixed, change saline density to 1020 kg/m³ and recalculate depth. Sketch a finite mixing zone, identify what the sharp-interface approximation predicts, and list additional pressure and salinity observations needed before any site-specific interpretation.","failure":"注意干擾：把四十倍比例當成任何海岸都固定成立的法則，會忽略密度、地層與流動的差異。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating a forty-to-one ratio as universal ignores density, stratigraphy and flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先以相同海面基準畫出兩側壓力柱，確認界面兩側壓力相等，再檢查密度和深度單位。比較分層鹽度剖面時，記錄混合帶厚度及採樣深度，將理想界面與實測過渡區分開呈現，不把一條計算線包裝成精確地質邊界。","textEn":"Draw pressure columns using one sea-level datum and verify pressure continuity before checking density and depth units. Compare depth-resolved salinity observations, recording mixing-zone thickness and sampling depth, and distinguish the ideal interface from the observed transition zone rather than presenting a calculated line as an exact geological boundary.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持淡水位不變，將鹹水密度改為1020 kg/m³並重算深度，再畫出有厚混合帶的剖面。說明哪個結果只是尖銳界面模型的預測，另列出需要補充的壓力與鹽度量測，避免把簡式直接當作場址設計。","textEn":"Hold freshwater head fixed, change saline density to 1020 kg/m³ and recalculate depth. Sketch a finite mixing zone, identify what the sharp-interface approximation predicts, and list additional pressure and salinity observations needed before any site-specific interpretation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「密度差與理想淡鹹水界面」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface\"?","options":["先以相同海面基準畫出兩側壓力柱，確認界面兩側壓力相等，再檢查密度和深度單位。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","觀測井一出現水位上升，就表示新注入水已經抵達該井，無需其他示蹤資料。"],"optionsEn":["Draw pressure columns using one sea-level datum and verify pressure continuity before checking density and depth units.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A water-level rise proves newly injected water has reached the well without any tracer evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先以相同海面基準畫出兩側壓力柱，確認界面兩側壓力相等，再檢查密度和深度單位。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw pressure columns using one sea-level datum and verify pressure continuity before checking density and depth units. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b298-v15-04","title":"密度差與理想淡鹹水界面：失效診斷","titleEn":"Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「密度差與理想淡鹹水界面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把四十倍比例當成任何海岸都固定成立的法則，會忽略密度、地層與流動的差異。抽水井附近可能出現局部鹽水上升，遠處水位看似足夠仍不能證明井口水質穩定。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating a forty-to-one ratio as universal ignores density, stratigraphy and flow. Local saltwater upconing near pumping wells may occur even when distant heads appear adequate, so a regional head measurement does not demonstrate stable production-water quality. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：實際評估需要同時觀察不同深度的壓力、鹽度和時間變化，不能只在單一水井量到高水位就認定所有含水層已受到保護。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assess pressure, salinity and temporal behavior at multiple depths instead of inferring protection from one high well level.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何海岸含水層只要水位高出海面一公尺，實際鹽水界面就必定精確位於四十公尺深。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every coastal aquifer with one metre of freshwater head has an actual interface exactly forty metres deep.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把四十倍比例當成任何海岸都固定成立的法則，會忽略密度、地層與流動的差異。抽水井附近可能出現局部鹽水上升，遠處水位看似足夠仍不能證明井口水質穩定。","textEn":"Treating a forty-to-one ratio as universal ignores density, stratigraphy and flow. Local saltwater upconing near pumping wells may occur even when distant heads appear adequate, so a regional head measurement does not demonstrate stable production-water quality.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「密度差與理想淡鹹水界面」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Density contrast and an ideal fresh-saline interface\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把四十倍比例當成任何海岸都固定成立的法則，會忽略密度、地層與流動的差異。","只要兩口井的水面高程相同，不論井內水的密度如何，壓力狀態就完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating a forty-to-one ratio as universal ignores density, stratigraphy and flow.","Equal water-surface elevations imply identical pressure conditions regardless of fluid density."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把四十倍比例當成任何海岸都固定成立的法則，會忽略密度、地層與流動的差異。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating a forty-to-one ratio as universal ignores density, stratigraphy and flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b298-v15-05","title":"等效淡水水頭與壓力基準：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「等效淡水水頭與壓力基準」如何影響地下水屏障防止海水入侵的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Groundwater barriers against seawater intrusion”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"井內水柱的密度會影響水位與壓力的換算，相同水面高程不一定表示相同的等效淡水水頭。使用壓力感測器時，必須清楚定義量測點高程、表壓或絕對壓以及參考密度，再把不同井的資料轉成一致表示方式。等效淡水水頭有助於比較壓力，但在密度隨位置改變時，不能把其梯度直接當成所有方向上的流速，尤其垂直方向還包含密度驅動項。海岸監測因此需要溫度和鹽度資料配合，讓壓力變化與密度變化能被分辨。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「等效淡水水頭與壓力基準」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water-column density affects conversion between pressure and level, so equal surface elevations need not imply equal equivalent freshwater heads. Define sensor elevation, gauge versus absolute pressure and reference density before comparing wells. Equivalent freshwater head provides a common pressure representation, but with spatially variable density its gradient alone does not describe flow in every direction; vertical flow includes an additional density effect. Coastal monitoring therefore needs temperature and salinity observations to distinguish pressure changes from changes in fluid density. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學量測點高程z=−20 m，表壓p=201105 Pa，參考淡水密度1000 kg/m³；h_f=z+p/(1000×9.81)=0.50 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For sensor elevation −20 m and gauge pressure 201105 Pa, freshwater-equivalent head is −20+201105/(1000×9.81)=0.50 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要兩口井的水面高程相同，不論井內水的密度如何，壓力狀態就完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal water-surface elevations imply identical pressure conditions regardless of fluid density.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「等效淡水水頭與壓力基準」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-05-k1","title":"等效淡水水頭與壓力基準","titleEn":"Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum","text":"井內水柱的密度會影響水位與壓力的換算，相同水面高程不一定表示相同的等效淡水水頭。使用壓力感測器時，必須清楚定義量測點高程、表壓或絕對壓以及參考密度，再把不同井的資料轉成一致表示方式。","textEn":"Water-column density affects conversion between pressure and level, so equal surface elevations need not imply equal equivalent freshwater heads. Define sensor elevation, gauge versus absolute pressure and reference density before comparing wells.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要兩口井的水面高程相同，不論井內水的密度如何，壓力狀態就完全相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal water-surface elevations imply identical pressure conditions regardless of fluid density. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「等效淡水水頭與壓力基準」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum\" is correct?","options":["只要兩口井的水面高程相同，不論井內水的密度如何，壓力狀態就完全相同。","達西通量與孔隙中的平均水流速度永遠相同，不需要知道有效孔隙率。","井內水柱的密度會影響水位與壓力的換算，相同水面高程不一定表示相同的等效淡水水頭。"],"optionsEn":["Equal water-surface elevations imply identical pressure conditions regardless of fluid density.","Darcy flux always equals average pore-water velocity without any need for effective porosity.","Water-column density affects conversion between pressure and level, so equal surface elevations need not imply equal equivalent freshwater heads."],"answer":2,"explanation":"井內水柱的密度會影響水位與壓力的換算，相同水面高程不一定表示相同的等效淡水水頭。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water-column density affects conversion between pressure and level, so equal surface elevations need not imply equal equivalent freshwater heads. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b298-v15-06","title":"等效淡水水頭與壓力基準：定量估算","titleEn":"Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「等效淡水水頭與壓力基準」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學量測點高程z=−20 m，表壓p=201105 Pa，參考淡水密度1000 kg/m³；h_f=z+p/(1000×9.81)=0.50 m。此壓力也等於密度1025 kg/m³、20 m鹹水柱的壓力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For sensor elevation −20 m and gauge pressure 201105 Pa, freshwater-equivalent head is −20+201105/(1000×9.81)=0.50 m. The pressure also equals that of a 20 m saline column at 1025 kg/m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：為每支感測器列出高程基準、壓力類型與密度來源，先扣除適當大氣壓再進行換算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record elevation datum, pressure type and density provenance for each instrument, applying the appropriate atmospheric correction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學量測點高程z=−20 m，表壓p=201105 Pa，參考淡水密度1000 kg/m³；h_f=z+p/(1000×9.81)=0.50 m。此壓力也等於密度1025 kg/m³、20 m鹹水柱的壓力。","textEn":"For sensor elevation −20 m and gauge pressure 201105 Pa, freshwater-equivalent head is −20+201105/(1000×9.81)=0.50 m. The pressure also equals that of a 20 m saline column at 1025 kg/m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「等效淡水水頭與壓力基準」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum\", which statement holds?","options":["教學量測點高程z=−20 m，表壓p=201105 Pa，參考淡水密度1000 kg/m³；h_f=z+p/(1000×9.81)=0.50 m。","兩個注入源各自造成的絕對水頭可以直接相加，不必扣除重複的背景水頭。","注入能力下降一定只代表細砂堵塞，因此不必檢查區域水位、密度或儀器校正。"],"optionsEn":["For sensor elevation −20 m and gauge pressure 201105 Pa, freshwater-equivalent head is −20+201105/(1000×9.81)=0.50 m.","Absolute heads from two injection sources can be added directly without removing duplicated background head.","Declining injectivity always means sand clogging, so regional head, density and calibration need no review."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學量測點高程z=−20 m，表壓p=201105 Pa，參考淡水密度1000 kg/m³；h_f=z+p/(1000×9.81)=0.50 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For sensor elevation −20 m and gauge pressure 201105 Pa, freshwater-equivalent head is −20+201105/(1000×9.81)=0.50 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b298-v15-07","title":"等效淡水水頭與壓力基準：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「等效淡水水頭與壓力基準」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"為每支感測器列出高程基準、壓力類型與密度來源，先扣除適當大氣壓再進行換算。用同一支儀器的人工水位與鹽度紀錄交叉檢查，對密度未知的時段標示不確定度，不能把資料缺口當成淡水條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record elevation datum, pressure type and density provenance for each instrument, applying the appropriate atmospheric correction. Cross-check against manual levels and salinity records, and flag uncertainty when density is unknown rather than silently assuming freshwater throughout a missing-data interval. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立淡水與鹹水兩根相同高度的虛擬水柱，分別計算底部表壓與等效淡水水頭。再加入一個不同高程的感測點，說明為何比較之前必須統一基準、壓力類型與密度，而非只比較畫面上的水位數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create equal-height virtual fresh and saline water columns and calculate bottom gauge pressure and equivalent freshwater head. Add a sensor at another elevation and explain why datum, pressure type and density must be reconciled before comparing displayed levels.","failure":"注意干擾：將絕對壓直接當表壓，會加入一整個大氣壓的偏差；將不同鹽度井的水面高程直接相減，則可能把密度差誤認為補注形成的梯度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using absolute pressure as gauge pressure adds an atmospheric offset. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"為每支感測器列出高程基準、壓力類型與密度來源，先扣除適當大氣壓再進行換算。用同一支儀器的人工水位與鹽度紀錄交叉檢查，對密度未知的時段標示不確定度，不能把資料缺口當成淡水條件。","textEn":"Record elevation datum, pressure type and density provenance for each instrument, applying the appropriate atmospheric correction. Cross-check against manual levels and salinity records, and flag uncertainty when density is unknown rather than silently assuming freshwater throughout a missing-data interval.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立淡水與鹹水兩根相同高度的虛擬水柱，分別計算底部表壓與等效淡水水頭。再加入一個不同高程的感測點，說明為何比較之前必須統一基準、壓力類型與密度，而非只比較畫面上的水位數字。","textEn":"Create equal-height virtual fresh and saline water columns and calculate bottom gauge pressure and equivalent freshwater head. Add a sensor at another elevation and explain why datum, pressure type and density must be reconciled before comparing displayed levels.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「等效淡水水頭與壓力基準」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","為每支感測器列出高程基準、壓力類型與密度來源，先扣除適當大氣壓再進行換算。","只要總注入量足夠，每個含水層就一定會自動獲得相同流量與相同保護。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Record elevation datum, pressure type and density provenance for each instrument, applying the appropriate atmospheric correction.","Adequate total injection automatically gives every aquifer equal flow and equal protection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"為每支感測器列出高程基準、壓力類型與密度來源，先扣除適當大氣壓再進行換算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record elevation datum, pressure type and density provenance for each instrument, applying the appropriate atmospheric correction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b298-v15-08","title":"等效淡水水頭與壓力基準：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「等效淡水水頭與壓力基準」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將絕對壓直接當表壓，會加入一整個大氣壓的偏差；將不同鹽度井的水面高程直接相減，則可能把密度差誤認為補注形成的梯度。兩種錯誤都可能改變對屏障成效的判斷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using absolute pressure as gauge pressure adds an atmospheric offset. Directly subtracting levels from wells with different salinities can mistake density effects for recharge gradients; either error can distort conclusions about barrier performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：海岸監測因此需要溫度和鹽度資料配合，讓壓力變化與密度變化能被分辨。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Coastal monitoring therefore needs temperature and salinity observations to distinguish pressure changes from changes in fluid density.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要兩口井的水面高程相同，不論井內水的密度如何，壓力狀態就完全相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal water-surface elevations imply identical pressure conditions regardless of fluid density.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將絕對壓直接當表壓，會加入一整個大氣壓的偏差；將不同鹽度井的水面高程直接相減，則可能把密度差誤認為補注形成的梯度。兩種錯誤都可能改變對屏障成效的判斷。","textEn":"Using absolute pressure as gauge pressure adds an atmospheric offset. Directly subtracting levels from wells with different salinities can mistake density effects for recharge gradients; either error can distort conclusions about barrier performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「等效淡水水頭與壓力基準」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equivalent freshwater head and pressure datum\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","達西通量與孔隙中的平均水流速度永遠相同，不需要知道有效孔隙率。","將絕對壓直接當表壓，會加入一整個大氣壓的偏差；將不同鹽度井的水面高程直接相減，則可能把密度差誤認為補注形成的梯度。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Darcy flux always equals average pore-water velocity without any need for effective porosity.","Using absolute pressure as gauge pressure adds an atmospheric offset."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將絕對壓直接當表壓，會加入一整個大氣壓的偏差；將不同鹽度井的水面高程直接相減，則可能把密度差誤認為補注形成的梯度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using absolute pressure as gauge pressure adds an atmospheric offset. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b298-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「達西通量與孔隙流速」與「理想徑向注入與水頭隆起」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Darcy flux and pore-water velocity\" and \"Ideal radial injection and head buildup\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b298-v15-09","title":"達西通量與孔隙流速：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Darcy flux and pore-water velocity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「達西通量與孔隙流速」如何影響地下水屏障防止海水入侵的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Darcy flux and pore-water velocity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Groundwater barriers against seawater intrusion”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"屏障改變水力梯度後，穿越含水層截面的流量可先用達西定律估算，但這個流量除以總截面積得到的是達西通量，不是水在孔隙中的平均前進速度。連通有效孔隙率決定可供流動的面積比例，使用總孔隙率或岩心小樣本值時都要注意代表性。此簡式假設單相、近似定密度、層流和可代表的水力傳導係數；若含水層有高導水通道，平均速度無法描述最快污染路徑。教學上應先分清流量、通量及速度，再討論旅行時間。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「達西通量與孔隙流速」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A changed hydraulic gradient can be translated into section flow using Darcy law, but discharge divided by total section area is Darcy flux rather than average pore-water velocity. Connected effective porosity determines the flowing fraction, and total porosity or a small core measurement may not represent it. The approximation assumes single-phase, approximately constant-density laminar flow and representative conductivity. Preferential pathways can move solute faster than the average, so distinguish discharge, flux and velocity before interpreting travel time. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Darcy flux and pore-water velocity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設K=20 m/day、梯度i=0.002、截面積A=500 m²及有效孔隙率0.25；Q=KiA=20 m³/day，達西通量0.04 m/day，平均孔隙流速0.04/0.25=0.16 m/day。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume conductivity 20 m/day, gradient 0.002, section area 500 m² and effective porosity 0.25.","failure":"常見誤解：「達西通量與孔隙中的平均水流速度永遠相同，不需要知道有效孔隙率。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Darcy flux always equals average pore-water velocity without any need for effective porosity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「達西通量與孔隙流速」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Darcy flux and pore-water velocity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-09-k1","title":"達西通量與孔隙流速","titleEn":"Darcy flux and pore-water velocity","text":"屏障改變水力梯度後，穿越含水層截面的流量可先用達西定律估算，但這個流量除以總截面積得到的是達西通量，不是水在孔隙中的平均前進速度。連通有效孔隙率決定可供流動的面積比例，使用總孔隙率或岩心小樣本值時都要注意代表性。","textEn":"A changed hydraulic gradient can be translated into section flow using Darcy law, but discharge divided by total section area is Darcy flux rather than average pore-water velocity. Connected effective porosity determines the flowing fraction, and total porosity or a small core measurement may not represent it.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：達西通量與孔隙中的平均水流速度永遠相同，不需要知道有效孔隙率。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Darcy flux always equals average pore-water velocity without any need for effective porosity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「達西通量與孔隙流速」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Darcy flux and pore-water velocity\" is correct?","options":["屏障改變水力梯度後，穿越含水層截面的流量可先用達西定律估算，但這個流量除以總截面積得到的是達西通量，不是水在孔隙中的平均前進速度。","達西通量與孔隙中的平均水流速度永遠相同，不需要知道有效孔隙率。","注入井內壓力升高多少，周圍所有觀測井的含水層水頭就必然同步升高多少。"],"optionsEn":["A changed hydraulic gradient can be translated into section flow using Darcy law, but discharge divided by total section area is Darcy flux rather than average pore-water velocity.","Darcy flux always equals average pore-water velocity without any need for effective porosity.","An injection-well pressure increase must appear unchanged at every surrounding observation well."],"answer":0,"explanation":"屏障改變水力梯度後，穿越含水層截面的流量可先用達西定律估算，但這個流量除以總截面積得到的是達西通量，不是水在孔隙中的平均前進速度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A changed hydraulic gradient can be translated into section flow using Darcy law, but discharge divided by total section area is Darcy flux rather than average pore-water velocity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b298-v15-10","title":"達西通量與孔隙流速：定量估算","titleEn":"Darcy flux and pore-water velocity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「達西通量與孔隙流速」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Darcy flux and pore-water velocity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設K=20 m/day、梯度i=0.002、截面積A=500 m²及有效孔隙率0.25；Q=KiA=20 m³/day，達西通量0.04 m/day，平均孔隙流速0.04/0.25=0.16 m/day。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume conductivity 20 m/day, gradient 0.002, section area 500 m² and effective porosity 0.25. Discharge is 20 m³/day, Darcy flux 0.04 m/day and average pore-water velocity 0.16 m/day. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐項標註量綱，檢查梯度是同基準水頭差除以距離，且截面方向與主要流向一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Label dimensions and confirm that gradient uses consistent head datums and distance, with area normal to flow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設K=20 m/day、梯度i=0.002、截面積A=500 m²及有效孔隙率0.25；Q=KiA=20 m³/day，達西通量0.04 m/day，平均孔隙流速0.04/0.25=0.16 m/day。","textEn":"Assume conductivity 20 m/day, gradient 0.002, section area 500 m² and effective porosity 0.25. Discharge is 20 m³/day, Darcy flux 0.04 m/day and average pore-water velocity 0.16 m/day.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「達西通量與孔隙流速」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Darcy flux and pore-water velocity\", which statement holds?","options":["只要樣本氯離子升高，就能單獨證明海水入侵，且不需要檢查其他來源。","教學假設K=20 m/day、梯度i=0.002、截面積A=500 m²及有效孔隙率0.25。","觀測井一出現水位上升，就表示新注入水已經抵達該井，無需其他示蹤資料。"],"optionsEn":["An increase in chloride alone proves seawater intrusion without checking any alternative source.","Assume conductivity 20 m/day, gradient 0.002, section area 500 m² and effective porosity 0.25.","A water-level rise proves newly injected water has reached the well without any tracer evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設K=20 m/day、梯度i=0.002、截面積A=500 m²及有效孔隙率0.25；Q=KiA=20 m³/day，達西通量0.04 m/day，平均孔隙流速0.04/0.25=0.16 m/day。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume conductivity 20 m/day, gradient 0.002, section area 500 m² and effective porosity 0.25. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b298-v15-11","title":"達西通量與孔隙流速：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Darcy flux and pore-water velocity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「達西通量與孔隙流速」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Darcy flux and pore-water velocity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐項標註量綱，檢查梯度是同基準水頭差除以距離，且截面方向與主要流向一致。以不同尺度的水力試驗和示蹤觀察比較有效參數，對只由單一岩心推估的速度另列限制，不把計算精度誤當現地參數精度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Label dimensions and confirm that gradient uses consistent head datums and distance, with area normal to flow. Compare hydraulic tests and tracer observations across scales, documenting limitations of core-derived parameters rather than confusing numerical precision with confidence in field conductivity or effective porosity. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持流量與截面不變，將有效孔隙率從0.25改為0.20，重算平均速度。再畫出一條高導水狹窄通道，解釋為何相同總流量可能產生不同的到達時間分布，並列出可辨識這種差異的觀測方式。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep discharge and section fixed while lowering effective porosity from 0.25 to 0.20. Recalculate velocity, sketch a narrow preferential pathway and explain why equal total discharge can produce different arrival-time distributions and require additional observations.","failure":"注意干擾：把流量除以總面積得到的值直接當成孔隙速度，會低估理想平均前進速度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating discharge per total area as pore velocity understates ideal average movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐項標註量綱，檢查梯度是同基準水頭差除以距離，且截面方向與主要流向一致。以不同尺度的水力試驗和示蹤觀察比較有效參數，對只由單一岩心推估的速度另列限制，不把計算精度誤當現地參數精度。","textEn":"Label dimensions and confirm that gradient uses consistent head datums and distance, with area normal to flow. Compare hydraulic tests and tracer observations across scales, documenting limitations of core-derived parameters rather than confusing numerical precision with confidence in field conductivity or effective porosity.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持流量與截面不變，將有效孔隙率從0.25改為0.20，重算平均速度。再畫出一條高導水狹窄通道，解釋為何相同總流量可能產生不同的到達時間分布，並列出可辨識這種差異的觀測方式。","textEn":"Keep discharge and section fixed while lowering effective porosity from 0.25 to 0.20. Recalculate velocity, sketch a narrow preferential pathway and explain why equal total discharge can produce different arrival-time distributions and require additional observations.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「達西通量與孔隙流速」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Darcy flux and pore-water velocity\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","地下水壓力呈現潮汐週期，就表示海水前緣每個週期都移動到相同的觀測位置。","逐項標註量綱，檢查梯度是同基準水頭差除以距離，且截面方向與主要流向一致。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A tidal pressure cycle proves that the seawater front reaches the observation location during every cycle.","Label dimensions and confirm that gradient uses consistent head datums and distance, with area normal to flow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐項標註量綱，檢查梯度是同基準水頭差除以距離，且截面方向與主要流向一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Label dimensions and confirm that gradient uses consistent head datums and distance, with area normal to flow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b298-v15-12","title":"達西通量與孔隙流速：失效診斷","titleEn":"Darcy flux and pore-water velocity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「達西通量與孔隙流速」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Darcy flux and pore-water velocity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把流量除以總面積得到的值直接當成孔隙速度，會低估理想平均前進速度。相反地，把有效孔隙率用得過小也會高估速度；通道效應則可能使兩種平均估算都無法描述最早到達。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating discharge per total area as pore velocity understates ideal average movement. An unrealistically small effective porosity overstates it, while preferential pathways can make either average insufficient for predicting earliest arrival at a monitoring point. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：教學上應先分清流量、通量及速度，再討論旅行時間。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Preferential pathways can move solute faster than the average, so distinguish discharge, flux and velocity before interpreting travel time.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「達西通量與孔隙中的平均水流速度永遠相同，不需要知道有效孔隙率。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Darcy flux always equals average pore-water velocity without any need for effective porosity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把流量除以總面積得到的值直接當成孔隙速度，會低估理想平均前進速度。相反地，把有效孔隙率用得過小也會高估速度；通道效應則可能使兩種平均估算都無法描述最早到達。","textEn":"Treating discharge per total area as pore velocity understates ideal average movement. An unrealistically small effective porosity overstates it, while preferential pathways can make either average insufficient for predicting earliest arrival at a monitoring point.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「達西通量與孔隙流速」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Darcy flux and pore-water velocity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把流量除以總面積得到的值直接當成孔隙速度，會低估理想平均前進速度。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","注入井內壓力升高多少，周圍所有觀測井的含水層水頭就必然同步升高多少。"],"optionsEn":["Treating discharge per total area as pore velocity understates ideal average movement.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","An injection-well pressure increase must appear unchanged at every surrounding observation well."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把流量除以總面積得到的值直接當成孔隙速度，會低估理想平均前進速度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating discharge per total area as pore velocity understates ideal average movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b298-v15-13","title":"理想徑向注入與水頭隆起：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ideal radial injection and head buildup: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「理想徑向注入與水頭隆起」如何影響地下水屏障防止海水入侵的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ideal radial injection and head buildup” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Groundwater barriers against seawater intrusion”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"在均質受壓含水層中，定常注入的水頭增量可由徑向流動近似理解，離注入位置越近，理想增量通常越大。公式中的外邊界不是任意選來配合答案的半徑，而是明確設定的定水頭邊界。穿透不完全、井皮效應、分層與密度差都會使現地反應偏離簡式；注入井內的壓力也不等於遠處含水層的水頭。因此本課僅用理想模型理解參數敏感度，不推導現場注入壓力設定或以單一井的反應取代監測網。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「理想徑向注入與水頭隆起」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In a homogeneous confined aquifer, steady radial flow explains how head buildup varies with distance from injection. The outer radius represents a specified constant-head boundary, not an arbitrary tuning distance. Partial penetration, well skin, layering and density contrast can invalidate the approximation, and pressure inside an injection well differs from aquifer head away from it. Use this ideal model for parameter sensitivity rather than prescribing operating pressure or substituting one well response for a distributed monitoring network. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ideal radial injection and head buildup” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設完全穿透、定常徑向流、T=100 m²/day、Q=500 m³/day，外定水頭半徑R=200 m；在r=10 m處Δh=Q ln(R/r)/(2πT)=2.384 m，忽略井損與密度差。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume fully penetrating steady radial injection, transmissivity 100 m²/day and discharge 500 m³/day, with constant-head radius 200 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「注入井內壓力升高多少，周圍所有觀測井的含水層水頭就必然同步升高多少。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An injection-well pressure increase must appear unchanged at every surrounding observation well.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「理想徑向注入與水頭隆起」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ideal radial injection and head buildup”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-13-k1","title":"理想徑向注入與水頭隆起","titleEn":"Ideal radial injection and head buildup","text":"在均質受壓含水層中，定常注入的水頭增量可由徑向流動近似理解，離注入位置越近，理想增量通常越大。公式中的外邊界不是任意選來配合答案的半徑，而是明確設定的定水頭邊界。","textEn":"In a homogeneous confined aquifer, steady radial flow explains how head buildup varies with distance from injection. The outer radius represents a specified constant-head boundary, not an arbitrary tuning distance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：注入井內壓力升高多少，周圍所有觀測井的含水層水頭就必然同步升高多少。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An injection-well pressure increase must appear unchanged at every surrounding observation well. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「理想徑向注入與水頭隆起」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ideal radial injection and head buildup\" is correct?","options":["注入井內壓力升高多少，周圍所有觀測井的含水層水頭就必然同步升高多少。","在均質受壓含水層中，定常注入的水頭增量可由徑向流動近似理解，離注入位置越近，理想增量通常越大。","兩個注入源各自造成的絕對水頭可以直接相加，不必扣除重複的背景水頭。"],"optionsEn":["An injection-well pressure increase must appear unchanged at every surrounding observation well.","In a homogeneous confined aquifer, steady radial flow explains how head buildup varies with distance from injection.","Absolute heads from two injection sources can be added directly without removing duplicated background head."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在均質受壓含水層中，定常注入的水頭增量可由徑向流動近似理解，離注入位置越近，理想增量通常越大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In a homogeneous confined aquifer, steady radial flow explains how head buildup varies with distance from injection. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b298-v15-14","title":"理想徑向注入與水頭隆起：定量估算","titleEn":"Ideal radial injection and head buildup: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「理想徑向注入與水頭隆起」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ideal radial injection and head buildup” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設完全穿透、定常徑向流、T=100 m²/day、Q=500 m³/day，外定水頭半徑R=200 m；在r=10 m處Δh=Q ln(R/r)/(2πT)=2.384 m，忽略井損與密度差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume fully penetrating steady radial injection, transmissivity 100 m²/day and discharge 500 m³/day, with constant-head radius 200 m. At radius 10 m, buildup is 500 ln(20)/(2π×100)=2.384 m, excluding well losses and density effects. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先在圖上標出外邊界和計算點，確認使用自然對數且半徑比無量綱。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark the outer boundary and evaluation point, checking natural logarithms and a dimensionless radius ratio.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設完全穿透、定常徑向流、T=100 m²/day、Q=500 m³/day，外定水頭半徑R=200 m；在r=10 m處Δh=Q ln(R/r)/(2πT)=2.384 m，忽略井損與密度差。","textEn":"Assume fully penetrating steady radial injection, transmissivity 100 m²/day and discharge 500 m³/day, with constant-head radius 200 m. At radius 10 m, buildup is 500 ln(20)/(2π×100)=2.384 m, excluding well losses and density effects.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「理想徑向注入與水頭隆起」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ideal radial injection and head buildup\", which statement holds?","options":["注入能力下降一定只代表細砂堵塞，因此不必檢查區域水位、密度或儀器校正。","只要總注入量足夠，每個含水層就一定會自動獲得相同流量與相同保護。","教學假設完全穿透、定常徑向流、T=100 m²/day、Q=500 m³/day，外定水頭半徑R=200 m。"],"optionsEn":["Declining injectivity always means sand clogging, so regional head, density and calibration need no review.","Adequate total injection automatically gives every aquifer equal flow and equal protection.","Assume fully penetrating steady radial injection, transmissivity 100 m²/day and discharge 500 m³/day, with constant-head radius 200 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設完全穿透、定常徑向流、T=100 m²/day、Q=500 m³/day，外定水頭半徑R=200 m；在r=10 m處Δh=Q ln(R/r)/(2πT)=2.384 m，忽略井損與密度差。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume fully penetrating steady radial injection, transmissivity 100 m²/day and discharge 500 m³/day, with constant-head radius 200 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b298-v15-15","title":"理想徑向注入與水頭隆起：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ideal radial injection and head buildup: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「理想徑向注入與水頭隆起」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ideal radial injection and head buildup” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先在圖上標出外邊界和計算點，確認使用自然對數且半徑比無量綱。將不同距離的增量畫成對數距離圖，再與觀測井而非注入井內壓力比較，若斜率或邊界反應不符，應重新檢查含水層與時間假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark the outer boundary and evaluation point, checking natural logarithms and a dimensionless radius ratio. Plot buildup against logarithmic distance and compare observation-well responses, not just injection-well pressure, revisiting aquifer and steady-state assumptions when the slope or boundary response differs. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將傳導係數加倍而保持注入量及邊界不變，重算水頭增量並畫出兩條理想剖面。接著加入一個只影響井內的假設井損，說明為何井壓上升不一定代表遠處屏障變強，並指出需要比較的量測位置。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double transmissivity while keeping injection and boundaries fixed, then compare ideal profiles. Add a hypothetical loss affecting only the injection well and explain why rising well pressure need not strengthen the distant barrier, identifying the observation locations required to distinguish both effects.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略井損而把注入井壓力全算成含水層水頭，會高估屏障向外延伸的效果。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assigning all injection-well pressure to aquifer buildup overstates the barrier effect away from the well. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先在圖上標出外邊界和計算點，確認使用自然對數且半徑比無量綱。將不同距離的增量畫成對數距離圖，再與觀測井而非注入井內壓力比較，若斜率或邊界反應不符，應重新檢查含水層與時間假設。","textEn":"Mark the outer boundary and evaluation point, checking natural logarithms and a dimensionless radius ratio. Plot buildup against logarithmic distance and compare observation-well responses, not just injection-well pressure, revisiting aquifer and steady-state assumptions when the slope or boundary response differs.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將傳導係數加倍而保持注入量及邊界不變，重算水頭增量並畫出兩條理想剖面。接著加入一個只影響井內的假設井損，說明為何井壓上升不一定代表遠處屏障變強，並指出需要比較的量測位置。","textEn":"Double transmissivity while keeping injection and boundaries fixed, then compare ideal profiles. Add a hypothetical loss affecting only the injection well and explain why rising well pressure need not strengthen the distant barrier, identifying the observation locations required to distinguish both effects.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「理想徑向注入與水頭隆起」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ideal radial injection and head buildup\"?","options":["先在圖上標出外邊界和計算點，確認使用自然對數且半徑比無量綱。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","任何海岸含水層只要水位高出海面一公尺，實際鹽水界面就必定精確位於四十公尺深。"],"optionsEn":["Mark the outer boundary and evaluation point, checking natural logarithms and a dimensionless radius ratio.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Every coastal aquifer with one metre of freshwater head has an actual interface exactly forty metres deep."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先在圖上標出外邊界和計算點，確認使用自然對數且半徑比無量綱。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark the outer boundary and evaluation point, checking natural logarithms and a dimensionless radius ratio. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b298-v15-16","title":"理想徑向注入與水頭隆起：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ideal radial injection and head buildup: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「理想徑向注入與水頭隆起」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ideal radial injection and head buildup” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略井損而把注入井壓力全算成含水層水頭，會高估屏障向外延伸的效果。尚未達定常時套用固定外邊界，也可能把時間造成的差異錯誤解讀成傳導係數改變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assigning all injection-well pressure to aquifer buildup overstates the barrier effect away from the well. Applying a fixed steady boundary before stabilization can likewise mistake time-dependent behavior for a change in aquifer transmissivity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此本課僅用理想模型理解參數敏感度，不推導現場注入壓力設定或以單一井的反應取代監測網。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Use this ideal model for parameter sensitivity rather than prescribing operating pressure or substituting one well response for a distributed monitoring network.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「注入井內壓力升高多少，周圍所有觀測井的含水層水頭就必然同步升高多少。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An injection-well pressure increase must appear unchanged at every surrounding observation well.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略井損而把注入井壓力全算成含水層水頭，會高估屏障向外延伸的效果。尚未達定常時套用固定外邊界，也可能把時間造成的差異錯誤解讀成傳導係數改變。","textEn":"Assigning all injection-well pressure to aquifer buildup overstates the barrier effect away from the well. Applying a fixed steady boundary before stabilization can likewise mistake time-dependent behavior for a change in aquifer transmissivity.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「理想徑向注入與水頭隆起」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ideal radial injection and head buildup\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","忽略井損而把注入井壓力全算成含水層水頭，會高估屏障向外延伸的效果。","兩個注入源各自造成的絕對水頭可以直接相加，不必扣除重複的背景水頭。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Assigning all injection-well pressure to aquifer buildup overstates the barrier effect away from the well.","Absolute heads from two injection sources can be added directly without removing duplicated background head."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略井損而把注入井壓力全算成含水層水頭，會高估屏障向外延伸的效果。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assigning all injection-well pressure to aquifer buildup overstates the barrier effect away from the well. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b298-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「線性疊加與井間薄弱區」與「保守離子與兩端元混合」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Linear superposition and gaps between wells\" and \"Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b298-v15-17","title":"線性疊加與井間薄弱區：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Linear superposition and gaps between wells: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「線性疊加與井間薄弱區」如何影響地下水屏障防止海水入侵的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Linear superposition and gaps between wells” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Groundwater barriers against seawater intrusion”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"在參數固定且控制方程線性的模型中，各注入源造成的水頭增量可以相加，但疊加的是同一基準下的增量，不是絕對水頭重複相加。井間位置可能比井邊的水頭低，因此屏障是否連續需要沿線剖面和深度分層來判讀。若飽和厚度顯著改變、密度耦合或井損非線性，簡單疊加便可能不適用。教學上應把背景水頭、各源增量與總水頭分開，讓學徒看出局部高值不能取代整條防護線的證據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「線性疊加與井間薄弱區」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When parameters are fixed and governing equations are linear, head increments from individual sources may be added. Add increments on one datum rather than repeatedly adding absolute heads. Interwell locations can have lower heads than locations near wells, so barrier continuity requires along-line and depth-resolved assessment. Changing saturated thickness, density coupling or nonlinear well losses may invalidate simple superposition. Separate background head, source increments and total head to show why a local maximum cannot establish protection along the entire barrier. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Linear superposition and gaps between wells” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設同一受壓線性模型、相同外邊界及固定參數，某點由兩注入源各產生1.5 m與1.0 m增量；合成增量2.5 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For one linear confined model with fixed properties and common boundaries, two sources add 1.5 and 1.0 m at a point.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩個注入源各自造成的絕對水頭可以直接相加，不必扣除重複的背景水頭。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Absolute heads from two injection sources can be added directly without removing duplicated background head.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「線性疊加與井間薄弱區」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Linear superposition and gaps between wells”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-17-k1","title":"線性疊加與井間薄弱區","titleEn":"Linear superposition and gaps between wells","text":"在參數固定且控制方程線性的模型中，各注入源造成的水頭增量可以相加，但疊加的是同一基準下的增量，不是絕對水頭重複相加。井間位置可能比井邊的水頭低，因此屏障是否連續需要沿線剖面和深度分層來判讀。","textEn":"When parameters are fixed and governing equations are linear, head increments from individual sources may be added. Add increments on one datum rather than repeatedly adding absolute heads.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩個注入源各自造成的絕對水頭可以直接相加，不必扣除重複的背景水頭。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Absolute heads from two injection sources can be added directly without removing duplicated background head. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「線性疊加與井間薄弱區」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Linear superposition and gaps between wells\" is correct?","options":["兩個注入源各自造成的絕對水頭可以直接相加，不必扣除重複的背景水頭。","只要樣本氯離子升高，就能單獨證明海水入侵，且不需要檢查其他來源。","在參數固定且控制方程線性的模型中，各注入源造成的水頭增量可以相加，但疊加的是同一基準下的增量，不是絕對水頭重複相加。"],"optionsEn":["Absolute heads from two injection sources can be added directly without removing duplicated background head.","An increase in chloride alone proves seawater intrusion without checking any alternative source.","When parameters are fixed and governing equations are linear, head increments from individual sources may be added."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在參數固定且控制方程線性的模型中，各注入源造成的水頭增量可以相加，但疊加的是同一基準下的增量，不是絕對水頭重複相加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When parameters are fixed and governing equations are linear, head increments from individual sources may be added. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b298-v15-18","title":"線性疊加與井間薄弱區：定量估算","titleEn":"Linear superposition and gaps between wells: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「線性疊加與井間薄弱區」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Linear superposition and gaps between wells” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設同一受壓線性模型、相同外邊界及固定參數，某點由兩注入源各產生1.5 m與1.0 m增量；合成增量2.5 m。背景水頭0.4 m時，總水頭2.9 m，而非把背景算兩次。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For one linear confined model with fixed properties and common boundaries, two sources add 1.5 and 1.0 m at a point. Total buildup is 2.5 m; adding background head 0.4 m once gives total head 2.9 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用單源與雙源模型在相同網格上比較水頭增量，檢查差值是否符合線性疊加。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare single-source and combined increments on the same grid to test linearity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設同一受壓線性模型、相同外邊界及固定參數，某點由兩注入源各產生1.5 m與1.0 m增量；合成增量2.5 m。背景水頭0.4 m時，總水頭2.9 m，而非把背景算兩次。","textEn":"For one linear confined model with fixed properties and common boundaries, two sources add 1.5 and 1.0 m at a point. Total buildup is 2.5 m; adding background head 0.4 m once gives total head 2.9 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「線性疊加與井間薄弱區」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Linear superposition and gaps between wells\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設同一受壓線性模型、相同外邊界及固定參數，某點由兩注入源各產生1.5 m與1.0 m增量；合成增量2.5 m。","觀測井一出現水位上升，就表示新注入水已經抵達該井，無需其他示蹤資料。","地下水壓力呈現潮汐週期，就表示海水前緣每個週期都移動到相同的觀測位置。"],"optionsEn":["For one linear confined model with fixed properties and common boundaries, two sources add 1.5 and 1.0 m at a point.","A water-level rise proves newly injected water has reached the well without any tracer evidence.","A tidal pressure cycle proves that the seawater front reaches the observation location during every cycle."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設同一受壓線性模型、相同外邊界及固定參數，某點由兩注入源各產生1.5 m與1.0 m增量；合成增量2.5 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For one linear confined model with fixed properties and common boundaries, two sources add 1.5 and 1.0 m at a point. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b298-v15-19","title":"線性疊加與井間薄弱區：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Linear superposition and gaps between wells: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「線性疊加與井間薄弱區」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Linear superposition and gaps between wells” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用單源與雙源模型在相同網格上比較水頭增量，檢查差值是否符合線性疊加。沿井間中線及不同深度列出最低值，並核對背景水頭是否只加入一次；對參數隨水頭改變的模型，另做完整聯合運算而非強行相加。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare single-source and combined increments on the same grid to test linearity. Examine interwell minima at multiple depths and verify that background head is added only once. When properties vary with head, use a combined calculation rather than forcing a linear sum onto a nonlinear system. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立五個沿線節點，分別給定兩源增量和同一背景水頭，算出總水頭並找最小值。將其中一源的流量降低一半，在線性假設下重算，再說明若含水層厚度同時改變，為何需要重新檢驗疊加條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create five along-line nodes with increments from two sources and one background head. Find the minimum total head, halve one source under linear assumptions, and explain why a simultaneous change in saturated thickness requires checking the superposition assumptions again.","failure":"注意干擾：只查看每口注入井旁的高水頭，可能漏掉井間或較深層的薄弱位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking only high heads beside injection wells can miss weaker interwell or deeper locations. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用單源與雙源模型在相同網格上比較水頭增量，檢查差值是否符合線性疊加。沿井間中線及不同深度列出最低值，並核對背景水頭是否只加入一次；對參數隨水頭改變的模型，另做完整聯合運算而非強行相加。","textEn":"Compare single-source and combined increments on the same grid to test linearity. Examine interwell minima at multiple depths and verify that background head is added only once. When properties vary with head, use a combined calculation rather than forcing a linear sum onto a nonlinear system.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立五個沿線節點，分別給定兩源增量和同一背景水頭，算出總水頭並找最小值。將其中一源的流量降低一半，在線性假設下重算，再說明若含水層厚度同時改變，為何需要重新檢驗疊加條件。","textEn":"Create five along-line nodes with increments from two sources and one background head. Find the minimum total head, halve one source under linear assumptions, and explain why a simultaneous change in saturated thickness requires checking the superposition assumptions again.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「線性疊加與井間薄弱區」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Linear superposition and gaps between wells\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","用單源與雙源模型在相同網格上比較水頭增量，檢查差值是否符合線性疊加。","只要兩口井的水面高程相同，不論井內水的密度如何，壓力狀態就完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare single-source and combined increments on the same grid to test linearity.","Equal water-surface elevations imply identical pressure conditions regardless of fluid density."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用單源與雙源模型在相同網格上比較水頭增量，檢查差值是否符合線性疊加。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare single-source and combined increments on the same grid to test linearity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b298-v15-20","title":"線性疊加與井間薄弱區：失效診斷","titleEn":"Linear superposition and gaps between wells: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「線性疊加與井間薄弱區」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Linear superposition and gaps between wells” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只查看每口注入井旁的高水頭，可能漏掉井間或較深層的薄弱位置。將絕對水頭相加又會重複背景值，造成整條屏障似乎比實際更高，進一步掩蓋監測配置不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking only high heads beside injection wells can miss weaker interwell or deeper locations. Adding absolute heads double-counts the background and exaggerates apparent protection, potentially concealing the need for a better distributed monitoring network. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：教學上應把背景水頭、各源增量與總水頭分開，讓學徒看出局部高值不能取代整條防護線的證據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Separate background head, source increments and total head to show why a local maximum cannot establish protection along the entire barrier.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩個注入源各自造成的絕對水頭可以直接相加，不必扣除重複的背景水頭。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Absolute heads from two injection sources can be added directly without removing duplicated background head.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只查看每口注入井旁的高水頭，可能漏掉井間或較深層的薄弱位置。將絕對水頭相加又會重複背景值，造成整條屏障似乎比實際更高，進一步掩蓋監測配置不足。","textEn":"Checking only high heads beside injection wells can miss weaker interwell or deeper locations. Adding absolute heads double-counts the background and exaggerates apparent protection, potentially concealing the need for a better distributed monitoring network.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「線性疊加與井間薄弱區」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Linear superposition and gaps between wells\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","只要樣本氯離子升高，就能單獨證明海水入侵，且不需要檢查其他來源。","只查看每口注入井旁的高水頭，可能漏掉井間或較深層的薄弱位置。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","An increase in chloride alone proves seawater intrusion without checking any alternative source.","Checking only high heads beside injection wells can miss weaker interwell or deeper locations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只查看每口注入井旁的高水頭，可能漏掉井間或較深層的薄弱位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking only high heads beside injection wells can miss weaker interwell or deeper locations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b298-v15-21","title":"保守離子與兩端元混合：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「保守離子與兩端元混合」如何影響地下水屏障防止海水入侵的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Groundwater barriers against seawater intrusion”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鹽度變化可以用保守溶質的兩端元混合先作概念估算，但必須確定淡水與海水端元濃度具有代表性，且沒有其他溶質來源、反應或顯著體積非加成。氯離子常被用來追蹤鹹水影響，卻也可能來自其他來源；一個濃度值不能獨自證明海水入侵。監測應結合離子比例、地層、時間序列與水力資訊，並明確區分混合比例、海水前緣位置和水質用途判斷，三者不是同一個計算問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「保守離子與兩端元混合」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Two-endmember conservative-solute mixing provides a conceptual estimate of saline contribution when freshwater and seawater concentrations are representative and other sources, reactions and volume nonadditivity are negligible. Chloride can trace saline influence but may have other origins, so one concentration does not independently demonstrate seawater intrusion. Combine ion ratios, stratigraphy, time series and hydraulic evidence. Distinguish mixing fraction from salt-front location and end-use water quality, because these are separate questions requiring different evidence. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設保守氯離子、體積可加，淡水50、海水19000、混合樣本240 mg/L；海水體積比例f=(240−50)/(19000−50)=0.010026，約1.003%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume conservative chloride and additive volumes, with fresh, sea and mixed concentrations of 50, 19000 and 240 mg/L.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要樣本氯離子升高，就能單獨證明海水入侵，且不需要檢查其他來源。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An increase in chloride alone proves seawater intrusion without checking any alternative source.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「保守離子與兩端元混合」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-21-k1","title":"保守離子與兩端元混合","titleEn":"Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing","text":"鹽度變化可以用保守溶質的兩端元混合先作概念估算，但必須確定淡水與海水端元濃度具有代表性，且沒有其他溶質來源、反應或顯著體積非加成。氯離子常被用來追蹤鹹水影響，卻也可能來自其他來源；一個濃度值不能獨自證明海水入侵。","textEn":"Two-endmember conservative-solute mixing provides a conceptual estimate of saline contribution when freshwater and seawater concentrations are representative and other sources, reactions and volume nonadditivity are negligible. Chloride can trace saline influence but may have other origins, so one concentration does not independently demonstrate seawater intrusion.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要樣本氯離子升高，就能單獨證明海水入侵，且不需要檢查其他來源。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An increase in chloride alone proves seawater intrusion without checking any alternative source. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「保守離子與兩端元混合」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing\" is correct?","options":["鹽度變化可以用保守溶質的兩端元混合先作概念估算，但必須確定淡水與海水端元濃度具有代表性，且沒有其他溶質來源、反應或顯著體積非加成。","只要樣本氯離子升高，就能單獨證明海水入侵，且不需要檢查其他來源。","注入能力下降一定只代表細砂堵塞，因此不必檢查區域水位、密度或儀器校正。"],"optionsEn":["Two-endmember conservative-solute mixing provides a conceptual estimate of saline contribution when freshwater and seawater concentrations are representative and other sources, reactions and volume nonadditivity are negligible.","An increase in chloride alone proves seawater intrusion without checking any alternative source.","Declining injectivity always means sand clogging, so regional head, density and calibration need no review."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鹽度變化可以用保守溶質的兩端元混合先作概念估算，但必須確定淡水與海水端元濃度具有代表性，且沒有其他溶質來源、反應或顯著體積非加成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Two-endmember conservative-solute mixing provides a conceptual estimate of saline contribution when freshwater and seawater concentrations are representative and other sources, reactions and volume nonadditivity are negligible. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b298-v15-22","title":"保守離子與兩端元混合：定量估算","titleEn":"Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「保守離子與兩端元混合」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設保守氯離子、體積可加，淡水50、海水19000、混合樣本240 mg/L；海水體積比例f=(240−50)/(19000−50)=0.010026，約1.003%。此值不代表用途合格或前緣位置。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume conservative chloride and additive volumes, with fresh, sea and mixed concentrations of 50, 19000 and 240 mg/L. Seawater volume fraction is (240−50)/(19000−50)=0.010026, about 1.003%, not a water-quality acceptance result or front location. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用質量守恆反代混合比例，檢查結果介於零與一之間，並將端元取樣日期和位置列入紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Substitute the fraction into mass balance, check that it lies between zero and one, and record endmember sampling dates and locations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設保守氯離子、體積可加，淡水50、海水19000、混合樣本240 mg/L；海水體積比例f=(240−50)/(19000−50)=0.010026，約1.003%。此值不代表用途合格或前緣位置。","textEn":"Assume conservative chloride and additive volumes, with fresh, sea and mixed concentrations of 50, 19000 and 240 mg/L. Seawater volume fraction is (240−50)/(19000−50)=0.010026, about 1.003%, not a water-quality acceptance result or front location.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「保守離子與兩端元混合」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing\", which statement holds?","options":["只要總注入量足夠，每個含水層就一定會自動獲得相同流量與相同保護。","教學假設保守氯離子、體積可加，淡水50、海水19000、混合樣本240 mg/L。","任何海岸含水層只要水位高出海面一公尺，實際鹽水界面就必定精確位於四十公尺深。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate total injection automatically gives every aquifer equal flow and equal protection.","Assume conservative chloride and additive volumes, with fresh, sea and mixed concentrations of 50, 19000 and 240 mg/L.","Every coastal aquifer with one metre of freshwater head has an actual interface exactly forty metres deep."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設保守氯離子、體積可加，淡水50、海水19000、混合樣本240 mg/L；海水體積比例f=(240−50)/(19000−50)=0.010026，約1.003%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume conservative chloride and additive volumes, with fresh, sea and mixed concentrations of 50, 19000 and 240 mg/L. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b298-v15-23","title":"保守離子與兩端元混合：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「保守離子與兩端元混合」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用質量守恆反代混合比例，檢查結果介於零與一之間，並將端元取樣日期和位置列入紀錄。再比較其他保守指標及水頭變化，若不同指標不能支持相同混合解釋，應調查額外來源或反應，而非只保留最符合預期的濃度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Substitute the fraction into mass balance, check that it lies between zero and one, and record endmember sampling dates and locations. Compare other conservative indicators and head changes; disagreement should prompt investigation of additional sources or reactions rather than selective retention of the preferred concentration. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將淡水端元濃度提高到100 mg/L，保持樣本與海水端元不變，重算比例。再加入第三個高氯來源的概念圖，說明單一濃度為何無法唯一分解三個來源，並提出至少一項額外觀測以改善辨識。","observationEn":"Site practice: Raise the freshwater endmember to 100 mg/L while retaining the other concentrations and recalculate the fraction. Add a third chloride source conceptually, explain why one concentration cannot uniquely separate three sources, and propose an additional observation that improves identification.","failure":"注意干擾：使用固定海水端元而忽略季節或河口淡化，會改變估算比例；若氯離子另有工業或地表來源，兩端元模型也可能把非海水污染誤認成海水混入，造成錯誤的成因判斷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A fixed seawater endmember can misrepresent seasonal or estuarine dilution. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用質量守恆反代混合比例，檢查結果介於零與一之間，並將端元取樣日期和位置列入紀錄。再比較其他保守指標及水頭變化，若不同指標不能支持相同混合解釋，應調查額外來源或反應，而非只保留最符合預期的濃度。","textEn":"Substitute the fraction into mass balance, check that it lies between zero and one, and record endmember sampling dates and locations. Compare other conservative indicators and head changes; disagreement should prompt investigation of additional sources or reactions rather than selective retention of the preferred concentration.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將淡水端元濃度提高到100 mg/L，保持樣本與海水端元不變，重算比例。再加入第三個高氯來源的概念圖，說明單一濃度為何無法唯一分解三個來源，並提出至少一項額外觀測以改善辨識。","textEn":"Raise the freshwater endmember to 100 mg/L while retaining the other concentrations and recalculate the fraction. Add a third chloride source conceptually, explain why one concentration cannot uniquely separate three sources, and propose an additional observation that improves identification.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「保守離子與兩端元混合」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","達西通量與孔隙中的平均水流速度永遠相同，不需要知道有效孔隙率。","用質量守恆反代混合比例，檢查結果介於零與一之間，並將端元取樣日期和位置列入紀錄。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Darcy flux always equals average pore-water velocity without any need for effective porosity.","Substitute the fraction into mass balance, check that it lies between zero and one, and record endmember sampling dates and locations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用質量守恆反代混合比例，檢查結果介於零與一之間，並將端元取樣日期和位置列入紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Substitute the fraction into mass balance, check that it lies between zero and one, and record endmember sampling dates and locations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b298-v15-24","title":"保守離子與兩端元混合：失效診斷","titleEn":"Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「保守離子與兩端元混合」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"使用固定海水端元而忽略季節或河口淡化，會改變估算比例；若氯離子另有工業或地表來源，兩端元模型也可能把非海水污染誤認成海水混入，造成錯誤的成因判斷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A fixed seawater endmember can misrepresent seasonal or estuarine dilution. Additional industrial or surface sources of chloride can be falsely assigned to seawater by a two-endmember model, producing an incorrect explanation of the observed concentration increase. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：監測應結合離子比例、地層、時間序列與水力資訊，並明確區分混合比例、海水前緣位置和水質用途判斷，三者不是同一個計算問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Distinguish mixing fraction from salt-front location and end-use water quality, because these are separate questions requiring different evidence.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要樣本氯離子升高，就能單獨證明海水入侵，且不需要檢查其他來源。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An increase in chloride alone proves seawater intrusion without checking any alternative source.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"使用固定海水端元而忽略季節或河口淡化，會改變估算比例；若氯離子另有工業或地表來源，兩端元模型也可能把非海水污染誤認成海水混入，造成錯誤的成因判斷。","textEn":"A fixed seawater endmember can misrepresent seasonal or estuarine dilution. Additional industrial or surface sources of chloride can be falsely assigned to seawater by a two-endmember model, producing an incorrect explanation of the observed concentration increase.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「保守離子與兩端元混合」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Conservative ions and two-endmember mixing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["使用固定海水端元而忽略季節或河口淡化，會改變估算比例；若氯離子另有工業或地表來源，兩端元模型也可能把非海水污染誤認成海水混入，造成錯誤的成因判斷。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","注入能力下降一定只代表細砂堵塞，因此不必檢查區域水位、密度或儀器校正。"],"optionsEn":["A fixed seawater endmember can misrepresent seasonal or estuarine dilution.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Declining injectivity always means sand clogging, so regional head, density and calibration need no review."],"answer":0,"explanation":"使用固定海水端元而忽略季節或河口淡化，會改變估算比例；若氯離子另有工業或地表來源，兩端元模型也可能把非海水污染誤認成海水混入，造成錯誤的成因判斷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A fixed seawater endmember can misrepresent seasonal or estuarine dilution. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b298-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「注入能力衰減與成因辨識」與「壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis\" and \"Pressure propagation versus solute travel time\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b298-v15-25","title":"注入能力衰減與成因辨識：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「注入能力衰減與成因辨識」如何影響地下水屏障防止海水入侵的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Groundwater barriers against seawater intrusion”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"注入能力常以流量除以相對背景的水頭增量描述，但指標下降不一定只有井周堵塞一種原因。區域水位升高、密度改變、量測位置差異或設備損失都可能改變分母，因此比較不同時間前應統一基準、流量區間與資料校正。堵塞也可能包含細粒、化學沉澱、生物膜與氣體效應，不能只用一個比值決定處理方式。課程以趨勢辨識為目的，要求先區分含水層反應和井內損失，再由具場址資料的人員評估原因。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「注入能力衰減與成因辨識」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Injectivity is commonly expressed as discharge divided by head buildup relative to background, but a decline does not uniquely diagnose clogging. Regional head changes, density, measurement location and equipment losses can alter the denominator, requiring consistent baselines, flow ranges and corrections. Clogging may involve particles, precipitation, biofilms or gas, and one ratio cannot select a remedy. Use the metric for trend detection, separating aquifer response from well losses before interpreting causes with site-specific evidence. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設同一流量100 m³/day，經背景與密度校正後的增量由2 m升至10 m；注入能力由50降至10 m²/day，降低80%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: At the same 100 m³/day flow, corrected buildup increases from 2 to 10 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「注入能力下降一定只代表細砂堵塞，因此不必檢查區域水位、密度或儀器校正。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Declining injectivity always means sand clogging, so regional head, density and calibration need no review.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「注入能力衰減與成因辨識」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-25-k1","title":"注入能力衰減與成因辨識","titleEn":"Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis","text":"注入能力常以流量除以相對背景的水頭增量描述，但指標下降不一定只有井周堵塞一種原因。區域水位升高、密度改變、量測位置差異或設備損失都可能改變分母，因此比較不同時間前應統一基準、流量區間與資料校正。","textEn":"Injectivity is commonly expressed as discharge divided by head buildup relative to background, but a decline does not uniquely diagnose clogging. Regional head changes, density, measurement location and equipment losses can alter the denominator, requiring consistent baselines, flow ranges and corrections.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：注入能力下降一定只代表細砂堵塞，因此不必檢查區域水位、密度或儀器校正。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Declining injectivity always means sand clogging, so regional head, density and calibration need no review. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「注入能力衰減與成因辨識」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis\" is correct?","options":["注入能力下降一定只代表細砂堵塞，因此不必檢查區域水位、密度或儀器校正。","注入能力常以流量除以相對背景的水頭增量描述，但指標下降不一定只有井周堵塞一種原因。","觀測井一出現水位上升，就表示新注入水已經抵達該井，無需其他示蹤資料。"],"optionsEn":["Declining injectivity always means sand clogging, so regional head, density and calibration need no review.","Injectivity is commonly expressed as discharge divided by head buildup relative to background, but a decline does not uniquely diagnose clogging.","A water-level rise proves newly injected water has reached the well without any tracer evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"注入能力常以流量除以相對背景的水頭增量描述，但指標下降不一定只有井周堵塞一種原因。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Injectivity is commonly expressed as discharge divided by head buildup relative to background, but a decline does not uniquely diagnose clogging. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b298-v15-26","title":"注入能力衰減與成因辨識：定量估算","titleEn":"Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「注入能力衰減與成因辨識」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設同一流量100 m³/day，經背景與密度校正後的增量由2 m升至10 m；注入能力由50降至10 m²/day，降低80%。這只是性能指標，不能據此直接提高現場注入壓力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: At the same 100 m³/day flow, corrected buildup increases from 2 to 10 m. Injectivity falls from 50 to 10 m²/day, an 80% decrease. This performance indicator does not justify increasing field injection pressure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對比同一流量區間、相同感測位置及一致背景基準的歷史資料，同時查看鄰近觀測井與注入井內的反應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare matching flow ranges, sensor locations and background datums while examining both injection and nearby observation wells.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設同一流量100 m³/day，經背景與密度校正後的增量由2 m升至10 m；注入能力由50降至10 m²/day，降低80%。這只是性能指標，不能據此直接提高現場注入壓力。","textEn":"At the same 100 m³/day flow, corrected buildup increases from 2 to 10 m. Injectivity falls from 50 to 10 m²/day, an 80% decrease. This performance indicator does not justify increasing field injection pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「注入能力衰減與成因辨識」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis\", which statement holds?","options":["地下水壓力呈現潮汐週期，就表示海水前緣每個週期都移動到相同的觀測位置。","只要兩口井的水面高程相同，不論井內水的密度如何，壓力狀態就完全相同。","教學假設同一流量100 m³/day，經背景與密度校正後的增量由2 m升至10 m；注入能力由50降至10 m²/day，降低80%。"],"optionsEn":["A tidal pressure cycle proves that the seawater front reaches the observation location during every cycle.","Equal water-surface elevations imply identical pressure conditions regardless of fluid density.","At the same 100 m³/day flow, corrected buildup increases from 2 to 10 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設同一流量100 m³/day，經背景與密度校正後的增量由2 m升至10 m；注入能力由50降至10 m²/day，降低80%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"At the same 100 m³/day flow, corrected buildup increases from 2 to 10 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b298-v15-27","title":"注入能力衰減與成因辨識：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「注入能力衰減與成因辨識」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對比同一流量區間、相同感測位置及一致背景基準的歷史資料，同時查看鄰近觀測井與注入井內的反應。把儀器校正、停運期間和水質變化標在時間軸上，區分量測偏差、區域變化與局部性能衰減的可能證據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare matching flow ranges, sensor locations and background datums while examining both injection and nearby observation wells. Mark calibration, shutdowns and source-water changes on the timeline to distinguish measurement bias, regional behavior and local performance deterioration using separate lines of evidence. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立兩份相同表面指標下降的合成紀錄，一份由背景水位變化造成，另一份由局部水頭損失增加造成。加入鄰近觀測井資料後重新計算，說明哪一項證據能區分兩種情境，以及哪些原因仍無法唯一確認。","observationEn":"Site practice: Construct two synthetic records with equal apparent injectivity decline, one caused by background head change and the other by local loss. Add nearby observation data, recalculate the corrected metric and identify which evidence distinguishes the scenarios and which causes remain unresolved.","failure":"注意干擾：直接比較未校正的井內壓力，可能把區域水位升高誤認成堵塞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Comparing uncorrected well pressures can mistake regional head rise for clogging. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對比同一流量區間、相同感測位置及一致背景基準的歷史資料，同時查看鄰近觀測井與注入井內的反應。把儀器校正、停運期間和水質變化標在時間軸上，區分量測偏差、區域變化與局部性能衰減的可能證據。","textEn":"Compare matching flow ranges, sensor locations and background datums while examining both injection and nearby observation wells. Mark calibration, shutdowns and source-water changes on the timeline to distinguish measurement bias, regional behavior and local performance deterioration using separate lines of evidence.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立兩份相同表面指標下降的合成紀錄，一份由背景水位變化造成，另一份由局部水頭損失增加造成。加入鄰近觀測井資料後重新計算，說明哪一項證據能區分兩種情境，以及哪些原因仍無法唯一確認。","textEn":"Construct two synthetic records with equal apparent injectivity decline, one caused by background head change and the other by local loss. Add nearby observation data, recalculate the corrected metric and identify which evidence distinguishes the scenarios and which causes remain unresolved.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「注入能力衰減與成因辨識」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis\"?","options":["對比同一流量區間、相同感測位置及一致背景基準的歷史資料，同時查看鄰近觀測井與注入井內的反應。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","注入井內壓力升高多少，周圍所有觀測井的含水層水頭就必然同步升高多少。"],"optionsEn":["Compare matching flow ranges, sensor locations and background datums while examining both injection and nearby observation wells.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","An injection-well pressure increase must appear unchanged at every surrounding observation well."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對比同一流量區間、相同感測位置及一致背景基準的歷史資料，同時查看鄰近觀測井與注入井內的反應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare matching flow ranges, sensor locations and background datums while examining both injection and nearby observation wells. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b298-v15-28","title":"注入能力衰減與成因辨識：失效診斷","titleEn":"Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「注入能力衰減與成因辨識」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"直接比較未校正的井內壓力，可能把區域水位升高誤認成堵塞。反過來，若只看流量仍達標而忽略所需水頭增加，可能錯失性能衰減的早期訊號，讓後續判讀更加困難。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Comparing uncorrected well pressures can mistake regional head rise for clogging. Conversely, observing unchanged discharge while ignoring increasing required head can miss early deterioration and leave later diagnosis dependent on incomplete historical records. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：課程以趨勢辨識為目的，要求先區分含水層反應和井內損失，再由具場址資料的人員評估原因。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Use the metric for trend detection, separating aquifer response from well losses before interpreting causes with site-specific evidence.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「注入能力下降一定只代表細砂堵塞，因此不必檢查區域水位、密度或儀器校正。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Declining injectivity always means sand clogging, so regional head, density and calibration need no review.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"直接比較未校正的井內壓力，可能把區域水位升高誤認成堵塞。反過來，若只看流量仍達標而忽略所需水頭增加，可能錯失性能衰減的早期訊號，讓後續判讀更加困難。","textEn":"Comparing uncorrected well pressures can mistake regional head rise for clogging. Conversely, observing unchanged discharge while ignoring increasing required head can miss early deterioration and leave later diagnosis dependent on incomplete historical records.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「注入能力衰減與成因辨識」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Declining injectivity and causal diagnosis\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","直接比較未校正的井內壓力，可能把區域水位升高誤認成堵塞。","觀測井一出現水位上升，就表示新注入水已經抵達該井，無需其他示蹤資料。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Comparing uncorrected well pressures can mistake regional head rise for clogging.","A water-level rise proves newly injected water has reached the well without any tracer evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"直接比較未校正的井內壓力，可能把區域水位升高誤認成堵塞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Comparing uncorrected well pressures can mistake regional head rise for clogging. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b298-v15-29","title":"壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pressure propagation versus solute travel time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間」如何影響地下水屏障防止海水入侵的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pressure propagation versus solute travel time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Groundwater barriers against seawater intrusion”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水頭訊號可以透過含水層的壓力擴散快速傳遞，而新注入水或溶質需要隨流動路徑前進，兩者的時間尺度常不同。觀測井很快出現水位反應，不代表補注水已到達或鹽水已被置換。壓力擴散的特徵時間取決於傳導係數與儲水係數，平流旅行時間則取決於孔隙速度和路徑長度；實際濃度曲線還受彌散和混合影響。解釋屏障監測時應把壓力、示蹤物與水質的證據分列，避免用快速訊號取代較慢的物質傳輸驗證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hydraulic signals can propagate through pressure diffusion much faster than injected water or solute moves along flow paths. A rapid well-level response does not demonstrate arrival of recharge water or displacement of salinity. Pressure timescales depend on transmissivity and storativity, whereas advective travel depends on pore velocity and path length; dispersion and mixing further shape concentration curves. Keep hydraulic, tracer and quality evidence separate so a fast pressure response is not substituted for slower verification of material transport. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pressure propagation versus solute travel time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設距離100 m、孔隙速度0.20 m/day，平流時間500日。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For distance 100 m and pore velocity 0.20 m/day, advective travel is 500 days.","failure":"常見誤解：「觀測井一出現水位上升，就表示新注入水已經抵達該井，無需其他示蹤資料。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A water-level rise proves newly injected water has reached the well without any tracer evidence.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pressure propagation versus solute travel time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-29-k1","title":"壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間","titleEn":"Pressure propagation versus solute travel time","text":"水頭訊號可以透過含水層的壓力擴散快速傳遞，而新注入水或溶質需要隨流動路徑前進，兩者的時間尺度常不同。觀測井很快出現水位反應，不代表補注水已到達或鹽水已被置換。","textEn":"Hydraulic signals can propagate through pressure diffusion much faster than injected water or solute moves along flow paths. A rapid well-level response does not demonstrate arrival of recharge water or displacement of salinity.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：觀測井一出現水位上升，就表示新注入水已經抵達該井，無需其他示蹤資料。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A water-level rise proves newly injected water has reached the well without any tracer evidence. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pressure propagation versus solute travel time\" is correct?","options":["觀測井一出現水位上升，就表示新注入水已經抵達該井，無需其他示蹤資料。","只要總注入量足夠，每個含水層就一定會自動獲得相同流量與相同保護。","水頭訊號可以透過含水層的壓力擴散快速傳遞，而新注入水或溶質需要隨流動路徑前進，兩者的時間尺度常不同。"],"optionsEn":["A water-level rise proves newly injected water has reached the well without any tracer evidence.","Adequate total injection automatically gives every aquifer equal flow and equal protection.","Hydraulic signals can propagate through pressure diffusion much faster than injected water or solute moves along flow paths."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水頭訊號可以透過含水層的壓力擴散快速傳遞，而新注入水或溶質需要隨流動路徑前進，兩者的時間尺度常不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hydraulic signals can propagate through pressure diffusion much faster than injected water or solute moves along flow paths. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b298-v15-30","title":"壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Pressure propagation versus solute travel time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pressure propagation versus solute travel time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設距離100 m、孔隙速度0.20 m/day，平流時間500日。若T=100 m²/day、S=0.001，水力擴散率D=T/S=100000 m²/day，尺度L²/D=0.10日；後者不是精確到達時間。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For distance 100 m and pore velocity 0.20 m/day, advective travel is 500 days. With transmissivity 100 m²/day and storativity 0.001, hydraulic diffusivity is 100000 m²/day and L²/D is 0.10 day, a characteristic scale rather than exact arrival time. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別繪製水頭與保守示蹤濃度的時間序列，統一時間基準但保留各自的採樣解析度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot head and conservative-tracer series on a common time basis while retaining their sampling resolutions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設距離100 m、孔隙速度0.20 m/day，平流時間500日。若T=100 m²/day、S=0.001，水力擴散率D=T/S=100000 m²/day，尺度L²/D=0.10日；後者不是精確到達時間。","textEn":"For distance 100 m and pore velocity 0.20 m/day, advective travel is 500 days. With transmissivity 100 m²/day and storativity 0.001, hydraulic diffusivity is 100000 m²/day and L²/D is 0.10 day, a characteristic scale rather than exact arrival time.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pressure propagation versus solute travel time\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設距離100 m、孔隙速度0.20 m/day，平流時間500日。","任何海岸含水層只要水位高出海面一公尺，實際鹽水界面就必定精確位於四十公尺深。","達西通量與孔隙中的平均水流速度永遠相同，不需要知道有效孔隙率。"],"optionsEn":["For distance 100 m and pore velocity 0.20 m/day, advective travel is 500 days.","Every coastal aquifer with one metre of freshwater head has an actual interface exactly forty metres deep.","Darcy flux always equals average pore-water velocity without any need for effective porosity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設距離100 m、孔隙速度0.20 m/day，平流時間500日。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For distance 100 m and pore velocity 0.20 m/day, advective travel is 500 days. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b298-v15-31","title":"壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure propagation versus solute travel time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pressure propagation versus solute travel time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別繪製水頭與保守示蹤濃度的時間序列，統一時間基準但保留各自的採樣解析度。檢查壓力反應是否也可能由潮汐或抽水造成，再以濃度和其他水化學證據辨識水體到達，不把第一個水位變化點當成示蹤物到達點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot head and conservative-tracer series on a common time basis while retaining their sampling resolutions. Check whether tides or pumping could explain the pressure response, then use concentration and supporting chemistry to assess water arrival instead of labeling the first head change as tracer breakthrough. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在同一張時間軸上標示兩種理想時間尺度，將孔隙速度降低一半再重算平流時間。另把儲水係數增加十倍，觀察壓力尺度如何改變，說明不同參數影響不同過程，不能用一個延遲係數同時校正所有資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Place both ideal timescales on one timeline, halve pore velocity and recalculate transport time. Increase storativity tenfold separately and compare the pressure scale, explaining why distinct processes respond to different parameters and cannot share one universal delay correction.","failure":"注意干擾：把快速水頭上升視為補注水已經到達，可能高估水質改善的速度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Equating rapid head rise with recharge-water arrival can overstate the speed of quality improvement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別繪製水頭與保守示蹤濃度的時間序列，統一時間基準但保留各自的採樣解析度。檢查壓力反應是否也可能由潮汐或抽水造成，再以濃度和其他水化學證據辨識水體到達，不把第一個水位變化點當成示蹤物到達點。","textEn":"Plot head and conservative-tracer series on a common time basis while retaining their sampling resolutions. Check whether tides or pumping could explain the pressure response, then use concentration and supporting chemistry to assess water arrival instead of labeling the first head change as tracer breakthrough.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在同一張時間軸上標示兩種理想時間尺度，將孔隙速度降低一半再重算平流時間。另把儲水係數增加十倍，觀察壓力尺度如何改變，說明不同參數影響不同過程，不能用一個延遲係數同時校正所有資料。","textEn":"Place both ideal timescales on one timeline, halve pore velocity and recalculate transport time. Increase storativity tenfold separately and compare the pressure scale, explaining why distinct processes respond to different parameters and cannot share one universal delay correction.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pressure propagation versus solute travel time\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","分別繪製水頭與保守示蹤濃度的時間序列，統一時間基準但保留各自的採樣解析度。","兩個注入源各自造成的絕對水頭可以直接相加，不必扣除重複的背景水頭。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Plot head and conservative-tracer series on a common time basis while retaining their sampling resolutions.","Absolute heads from two injection sources can be added directly without removing duplicated background head."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分別繪製水頭與保守示蹤濃度的時間序列，統一時間基準但保留各自的採樣解析度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot head and conservative-tracer series on a common time basis while retaining their sampling resolutions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b298-v15-32","title":"壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pressure propagation versus solute travel time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pressure propagation versus solute travel time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把快速水頭上升視為補注水已經到達，可能高估水質改善的速度。若示蹤物尚未量到就判定工程失效，也可能忽略較長旅行時間；兩種誤判都源於把壓力與物質傳輸混成同一過程。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Equating rapid head rise with recharge-water arrival can overstate the speed of quality improvement. Declaring failure before tracer arrival can instead ignore a longer travel time; both errors confuse pressure transmission with movement of water and solute. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋屏障監測時應把壓力、示蹤物與水質的證據分列，避免用快速訊號取代較慢的物質傳輸驗證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Keep hydraulic, tracer and quality evidence separate so a fast pressure response is not substituted for slower verification of material transport.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「觀測井一出現水位上升，就表示新注入水已經抵達該井，無需其他示蹤資料。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A water-level rise proves newly injected water has reached the well without any tracer evidence.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把快速水頭上升視為補注水已經到達，可能高估水質改善的速度。若示蹤物尚未量到就判定工程失效，也可能忽略較長旅行時間；兩種誤判都源於把壓力與物質傳輸混成同一過程。","textEn":"Equating rapid head rise with recharge-water arrival can overstate the speed of quality improvement. Declaring failure before tracer arrival can instead ignore a longer travel time; both errors confuse pressure transmission with movement of water and solute.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓力傳播與溶質旅行時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pressure propagation versus solute travel time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要總注入量足夠，每個含水層就一定會自動獲得相同流量與相同保護。","把快速水頭上升視為補注水已經到達，可能高估水質改善的速度。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Adequate total injection automatically gives every aquifer equal flow and equal protection.","Equating rapid head rise with recharge-water arrival can overstate the speed of quality improvement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把快速水頭上升視為補注水已經到達，可能高估水質改善的速度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Equating rapid head rise with recharge-water arrival can overstate the speed of quality improvement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b298-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「分層分配與獨立含水層」與「潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Layer allocation and independent aquifers\" and \"Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b298-v15-33","title":"分層分配與獨立含水層：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Layer allocation and independent aquifers: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「分層分配與獨立含水層」如何影響地下水屏障防止海水入侵的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Layer allocation and independent aquifers” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Groundwater barriers against seawater intrusion”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多層含水層的補注分配取決於各層傳導能力、背景水頭與施加增量。即使總流量足夠，也可能主要進入較高傳導性的層位，讓其他層的防護不足。教學模型可把兩個彼此隔離、相同幾何的線性支路放在紙上比較，但不能據此設計跨層連通井，因為實際層間混流會改變水質與壓力邊界。分析應保留每層獨立的水量帳和監測資料，避免把全井平均反應當成各層反應一致的證據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分層分配與獨立含水層」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Recharge allocation across layers depends on transmissivity, background head and imposed buildup. Sufficient total flow may preferentially enter a conductive layer while another remains weakly supported. A teaching model can compare hydraulically isolated linear branches with equal geometry, but it does not justify cross-aquifer connections, which alter quality and pressure boundaries. Keep separate layer balances and monitoring evidence instead of treating an average well response as proof that every aquifer receives equal hydraulic protection. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Layer allocation and independent aquifers” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設兩個水力隔離支路，幾何、外邊界和施加增量相同，T分別100與50 m²/day；總Q=300 m³/day依傳導係數比例分為200與100 m³/day。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For two hydraulically isolated branches with equal geometry, outer heads and applied buildup, transmissivities are 100 and 50 m²/day.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要總注入量足夠，每個含水層就一定會自動獲得相同流量與相同保護。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate total injection automatically gives every aquifer equal flow and equal protection.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分層分配與獨立含水層」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Layer allocation and independent aquifers”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-33-k1","title":"分層分配與獨立含水層","titleEn":"Layer allocation and independent aquifers","text":"多層含水層的補注分配取決於各層傳導能力、背景水頭與施加增量。即使總流量足夠，也可能主要進入較高傳導性的層位，讓其他層的防護不足。","textEn":"Recharge allocation across layers depends on transmissivity, background head and imposed buildup. Sufficient total flow may preferentially enter a conductive layer while another remains weakly supported.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要總注入量足夠，每個含水層就一定會自動獲得相同流量與相同保護。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate total injection automatically gives every aquifer equal flow and equal protection. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分層分配與獨立含水層」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Layer allocation and independent aquifers\" is correct?","options":["多層含水層的補注分配取決於各層傳導能力、背景水頭與施加增量。","只要總注入量足夠，每個含水層就一定會自動獲得相同流量與相同保護。","地下水壓力呈現潮汐週期，就表示海水前緣每個週期都移動到相同的觀測位置。"],"optionsEn":["Recharge allocation across layers depends on transmissivity, background head and imposed buildup.","Adequate total injection automatically gives every aquifer equal flow and equal protection.","A tidal pressure cycle proves that the seawater front reaches the observation location during every cycle."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多層含水層的補注分配取決於各層傳導能力、背景水頭與施加增量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Recharge allocation across layers depends on transmissivity, background head and imposed buildup. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b298-v15-34","title":"分層分配與獨立含水層：定量估算","titleEn":"Layer allocation and independent aquifers: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分層分配與獨立含水層」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Layer allocation and independent aquifers” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設兩個水力隔離支路，幾何、外邊界和施加增量相同，T分別100與50 m²/day；總Q=300 m³/day依傳導係數比例分為200與100 m³/day。僅為獨立支路線性模型。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For two hydraulically isolated branches with equal geometry, outer heads and applied buildup, transmissivities are 100 and 50 m²/day. A total 300 m³/day splits proportionally into 200 and 100 m³/day in this linear teaching model. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先檢查兩支路是否確實採相同邊界與幾何，再分別核對流量和水頭資料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify common geometry and boundary assumptions before comparing branch flows and heads.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設兩個水力隔離支路，幾何、外邊界和施加增量相同，T分別100與50 m²/day；總Q=300 m³/day依傳導係數比例分為200與100 m³/day。僅為獨立支路線性模型。","textEn":"For two hydraulically isolated branches with equal geometry, outer heads and applied buildup, transmissivities are 100 and 50 m²/day. A total 300 m³/day splits proportionally into 200 and 100 m³/day in this linear teaching model.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分層分配與獨立含水層」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Layer allocation and independent aquifers\", which statement holds?","options":["只要兩口井的水面高程相同，不論井內水的密度如何，壓力狀態就完全相同。","教學假設兩個水力隔離支路，幾何、外邊界和施加增量相同，T分別100與50 m²/day。","注入井內壓力升高多少，周圍所有觀測井的含水層水頭就必然同步升高多少。"],"optionsEn":["Equal water-surface elevations imply identical pressure conditions regardless of fluid density.","For two hydraulically isolated branches with equal geometry, outer heads and applied buildup, transmissivities are 100 and 50 m²/day.","An injection-well pressure increase must appear unchanged at every surrounding observation well."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設兩個水力隔離支路，幾何、外邊界和施加增量相同，T分別100與50 m²/day；總Q=300 m³/day依傳導係數比例分為200與100 m³/day。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For two hydraulically isolated branches with equal geometry, outer heads and applied buildup, transmissivities are 100 and 50 m²/day. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b298-v15-35","title":"分層分配與獨立含水層：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Layer allocation and independent aquifers: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分層分配與獨立含水層」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Layer allocation and independent aquifers” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先檢查兩支路是否確實採相同邊界與幾何，再分別核對流量和水頭資料。以分層觀測而非全井平均濃度判讀防護效果，若背景水頭不同，需重新解各支路方程，不可仍用傳導係數比例硬分總流量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify common geometry and boundary assumptions before comparing branch flows and heads. Assess protection with layer-specific observations rather than whole-well average concentration. If background heads differ, solve the branches separately instead of retaining a proportional split based only on transmissivity. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將第二支路的傳導係數降為25 m²/day，在相同線性邊界下重算分配。再只改其背景水頭，指出原本比例式哪個假設不再成立，並畫出應分層記錄的流量、水頭和鹽度欄位，不提出實體跨層接通方案。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce the second branch transmissivity to 25 m²/day and recalculate the split under unchanged linear boundaries. Then change only its background head, identify the failed assumption and design separate flow, head and salinity records without proposing physical cross-aquifer connections.","failure":"注意干擾：把總注入量平均除以層數，會忽略各層傳導能力不同。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Dividing total injection equally among layers ignores differing transmissivity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先檢查兩支路是否確實採相同邊界與幾何，再分別核對流量和水頭資料。以分層觀測而非全井平均濃度判讀防護效果，若背景水頭不同，需重新解各支路方程，不可仍用傳導係數比例硬分總流量。","textEn":"Verify common geometry and boundary assumptions before comparing branch flows and heads. Assess protection with layer-specific observations rather than whole-well average concentration. If background heads differ, solve the branches separately instead of retaining a proportional split based only on transmissivity.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將第二支路的傳導係數降為25 m²/day，在相同線性邊界下重算分配。再只改其背景水頭，指出原本比例式哪個假設不再成立，並畫出應分層記錄的流量、水頭和鹽度欄位，不提出實體跨層接通方案。","textEn":"Reduce the second branch transmissivity to 25 m²/day and recalculate the split under unchanged linear boundaries. Then change only its background head, identify the failed assumption and design separate flow, head and salinity records without proposing physical cross-aquifer connections.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分層分配與獨立含水層」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Layer allocation and independent aquifers\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要樣本氯離子升高，就能單獨證明海水入侵，且不需要檢查其他來源。","先檢查兩支路是否確實採相同邊界與幾何，再分別核對流量和水頭資料。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","An increase in chloride alone proves seawater intrusion without checking any alternative source.","Verify common geometry and boundary assumptions before comparing branch flows and heads."],"answer":2,"explanation":"先檢查兩支路是否確實採相同邊界與幾何，再分別核對流量和水頭資料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify common geometry and boundary assumptions before comparing branch flows and heads. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b298-v15-36","title":"分層分配與獨立含水層：失效診斷","titleEn":"Layer allocation and independent aquifers: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分層分配與獨立含水層」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Layer allocation and independent aquifers” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把總注入量平均除以層數，會忽略各層傳導能力不同。若高流量層的淡水掩蓋另一層鹽度升高，全井混合樣本可能看似穩定，卻無法揭示較弱層位的變化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Dividing total injection equally among layers ignores differing transmissivity. Fresh water from a high-flow layer can mask rising salinity in another, so a stable mixed well sample may conceal important changes within a weaker layer. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：分析應保留每層獨立的水量帳和監測資料，避免把全井平均反應當成各層反應一致的證據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Keep separate layer balances and monitoring evidence instead of treating an average well response as proof that every aquifer receives equal hydraulic protection.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要總注入量足夠，每個含水層就一定會自動獲得相同流量與相同保護。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate total injection automatically gives every aquifer equal flow and equal protection.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把總注入量平均除以層數，會忽略各層傳導能力不同。若高流量層的淡水掩蓋另一層鹽度升高，全井混合樣本可能看似穩定，卻無法揭示較弱層位的變化。","textEn":"Dividing total injection equally among layers ignores differing transmissivity. Fresh water from a high-flow layer can mask rising salinity in another, so a stable mixed well sample may conceal important changes within a weaker layer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分層分配與獨立含水層」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Layer allocation and independent aquifers\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把總注入量平均除以層數，會忽略各層傳導能力不同。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","地下水壓力呈現潮汐週期，就表示海水前緣每個週期都移動到相同的觀測位置。"],"optionsEn":["Dividing total injection equally among layers ignores differing transmissivity.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A tidal pressure cycle proves that the seawater front reaches the observation location during every cycle."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把總注入量平均除以層數，會忽略各層傳導能力不同。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dividing total injection equally among layers ignores differing transmissivity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b298-v15-37","title":"潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲」如何影響地下水屏障防止海水入侵的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Groundwater barriers against seawater intrusion”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海岸潮汐可使地下水壓力週期變化，離岸距離增加時振幅可能衰減並產生相位延遲。這種訊號提供水力參數的線索，但壓力潮汐並不等於鹽水隨每個週期同距離進退。理想一維受壓半無限含水層可以用擴散方程的週期解描述，實際上地層邊界、河道、抽水與大氣壓都可能疊加其他訊號。學徒應先理解振幅比和相位的量綱，再以多點資料檢查模型是否合理，而不是只用一口井擬合出漂亮曲線就宣稱掌握入侵範圍。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Coastal tides can drive periodic groundwater pressure with attenuation and phase delay inland. These signals inform hydraulic behavior but do not mean saltwater moves the same distance each cycle. A one-dimensional semi-infinite confined aquifer has an ideal periodic diffusion solution; boundaries, channels, pumping and atmospheric pressure introduce additional signals in practice. Understand amplitude ratios and phase dimensions, then compare multiple observations rather than treating a good fit at one well as proof of the saltwater-intrusion extent. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設一維受壓半無限含水層，D=10000 m²/day、潮週期0.50 day；ω=2π/0.50，衰減長度δ=√(2D/ω)=39.894 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For an ideal one-dimensional semi-infinite confined aquifer, diffusivity 10000 m²/day and period 0.50 day give angular frequency 2π/0.50 and attenuation length 39.894 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「地下水壓力呈現潮汐週期，就表示海水前緣每個週期都移動到相同的觀測位置。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A tidal pressure cycle proves that the seawater front reaches the observation location during every cycle.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-37-k1","title":"潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲","titleEn":"Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag","text":"海岸潮汐可使地下水壓力週期變化，離岸距離增加時振幅可能衰減並產生相位延遲。這種訊號提供水力參數的線索，但壓力潮汐並不等於鹽水隨每個週期同距離進退。","textEn":"Coastal tides can drive periodic groundwater pressure with attenuation and phase delay inland. These signals inform hydraulic behavior but do not mean saltwater moves the same distance each cycle.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地下水壓力呈現潮汐週期，就表示海水前緣每個週期都移動到相同的觀測位置。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A tidal pressure cycle proves that the seawater front reaches the observation location during every cycle. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag\" is correct?","options":["地下水壓力呈現潮汐週期，就表示海水前緣每個週期都移動到相同的觀測位置。","海岸潮汐可使地下水壓力週期變化，離岸距離增加時振幅可能衰減並產生相位延遲。","任何海岸含水層只要水位高出海面一公尺，實際鹽水界面就必定精確位於四十公尺深。"],"optionsEn":["A tidal pressure cycle proves that the seawater front reaches the observation location during every cycle.","Coastal tides can drive periodic groundwater pressure with attenuation and phase delay inland.","Every coastal aquifer with one metre of freshwater head has an actual interface exactly forty metres deep."],"answer":1,"explanation":"海岸潮汐可使地下水壓力週期變化，離岸距離增加時振幅可能衰減並產生相位延遲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Coastal tides can drive periodic groundwater pressure with attenuation and phase delay inland. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b298-v15-38","title":"潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲：定量估算","titleEn":"Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設一維受壓半無限含水層，D=10000 m²/day、潮週期0.50 day；ω=2π/0.50，衰減長度δ=√(2D/ω)=39.894 m。在x=40 m，振幅比exp(−x/δ)=0.3669，相位延遲1.0027 rad。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For an ideal one-dimensional semi-infinite confined aquifer, diffusivity 10000 m²/day and period 0.50 day give angular frequency 2π/0.50 and attenuation length 39.894 m. At 40 m, amplitude ratio is 0.3669 and phase lag 1.0027 radians. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對潮位與井壓時間戳及取樣頻率，以相同週期分量比較振幅和相位，避免把日平均資料拿來解半日潮。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check tide and well-pressure timestamps and sampling frequency, comparing the same periodic component rather than applying daily averages to semidiurnal tides.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設一維受壓半無限含水層，D=10000 m²/day、潮週期0.50 day；ω=2π/0.50，衰減長度δ=√(2D/ω)=39.894 m。在x=40 m，振幅比exp(−x/δ)=0.3669，相位延遲1.0027 rad。","textEn":"For an ideal one-dimensional semi-infinite confined aquifer, diffusivity 10000 m²/day and period 0.50 day give angular frequency 2π/0.50 and attenuation length 39.894 m. At 40 m, amplitude ratio is 0.3669 and phase lag 1.0027 radians.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag\", which statement holds?","options":["達西通量與孔隙中的平均水流速度永遠相同，不需要知道有效孔隙率。","兩個注入源各自造成的絕對水頭可以直接相加，不必扣除重複的背景水頭。","教學假設一維受壓半無限含水層，D=10000 m²/day、潮週期0.50 day；ω=2π/0.50，衰減長度δ=√(2D/ω)=39.894 m。"],"optionsEn":["Darcy flux always equals average pore-water velocity without any need for effective porosity.","Absolute heads from two injection sources can be added directly without removing duplicated background head.","For an ideal one-dimensional semi-infinite confined aquifer, diffusivity 10000 m²/day and period 0.50 day give angular frequency 2π/0.50 and attenuation length 39.894 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設一維受壓半無限含水層，D=10000 m²/day、潮週期0.50 day；ω=2π/0.50，衰減長度δ=√(2D/ω)=39.894 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For an ideal one-dimensional semi-infinite confined aquifer, diffusivity 10000 m²/day and period 0.50 day give angular frequency 2π/0.50 and attenuation length 39.894 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b298-v15-39","title":"潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對潮位與井壓時間戳及取樣頻率，以相同週期分量比較振幅和相位，避免把日平均資料拿來解半日潮。再檢查多個距離的衰減是否一致，並將抽水及大氣壓紀錄列為競爭解釋，確認擬合不是時間錯位造成。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check tide and well-pressure timestamps and sampling frequency, comparing the same periodic component rather than applying daily averages to semidiurnal tides. Examine attenuation across multiple distances and consider pumping and atmospheric pressure as alternative explanations, verifying that apparent phase lag is not merely clock error. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把潮週期加倍，保持擴散率和距離不變，重算衰減長度、振幅比與相位。另加入十分鐘時鐘偏差，換算造成的相位誤差，說明資料同步與物理參數估計之間的關係，並區分壓力模型與鹽度驗證。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double tidal period with diffusivity and distance fixed, recalculating attenuation length, amplitude ratio and phase. Add a ten-minute clock offset and convert it to phase error, explaining how synchronization affects inference while keeping hydraulic modeling distinct from salinity verification.","failure":"注意干擾：不同儀器時鐘未同步，會產生假的相位延遲，進而扭曲推估的擴散率。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unsynchronized clocks create artificial phase lag and distort inferred diffusivity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對潮位與井壓時間戳及取樣頻率，以相同週期分量比較振幅和相位，避免把日平均資料拿來解半日潮。再檢查多個距離的衰減是否一致，並將抽水及大氣壓紀錄列為競爭解釋，確認擬合不是時間錯位造成。","textEn":"Check tide and well-pressure timestamps and sampling frequency, comparing the same periodic component rather than applying daily averages to semidiurnal tides. Examine attenuation across multiple distances and consider pumping and atmospheric pressure as alternative explanations, verifying that apparent phase lag is not merely clock error.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把潮週期加倍，保持擴散率和距離不變，重算衰減長度、振幅比與相位。另加入十分鐘時鐘偏差，換算造成的相位誤差，說明資料同步與物理參數估計之間的關係，並區分壓力模型與鹽度驗證。","textEn":"Double tidal period with diffusivity and distance fixed, recalculating attenuation length, amplitude ratio and phase. Add a ten-minute clock offset and convert it to phase error, explaining how synchronization affects inference while keeping hydraulic modeling distinct from salinity verification.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag\"?","options":["核對潮位與井壓時間戳及取樣頻率，以相同週期分量比較振幅和相位，避免把日平均資料拿來解半日潮。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","注入能力下降一定只代表細砂堵塞，因此不必檢查區域水位、密度或儀器校正。"],"optionsEn":["Check tide and well-pressure timestamps and sampling frequency, comparing the same periodic component rather than applying daily averages to semidiurnal tides.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Declining injectivity always means sand clogging, so regional head, density and calibration need no review."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對潮位與井壓時間戳及取樣頻率，以相同週期分量比較振幅和相位，避免把日平均資料拿來解半日潮。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check tide and well-pressure timestamps and sampling frequency, comparing the same periodic component rather than applying daily averages to semidiurnal tides. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b298-v15-40","title":"潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"prerequisiteIds":["b298-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同儀器時鐘未同步，會產生假的相位延遲，進而扭曲推估的擴散率。即使壓力週期擬合良好，也不能省略鹽度監測，因為壓力訊號與溶質前緣屬於不同的物理過程。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unsynchronized clocks create artificial phase lag and distort inferred diffusivity. Even a strong pressure-cycle fit cannot replace salinity monitoring, because hydraulic signals and solute fronts describe different physical processes and require distinct supporting observations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：學徒應先理解振幅比和相位的量綱，再以多點資料檢查模型是否合理，而不是只用一口井擬合出漂亮曲線就宣稱掌握入侵範圍。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Understand amplitude ratios and phase dimensions, then compare multiple observations rather than treating a good fit at one well as proof of the saltwater-intrusion extent.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地下水壓力呈現潮汐週期，就表示海水前緣每個週期都移動到相同的觀測位置。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A tidal pressure cycle proves that the seawater front reaches the observation location during every cycle.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b298-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同儀器時鐘未同步，會產生假的相位延遲，進而扭曲推估的擴散率。即使壓力週期擬合良好，也不能省略鹽度監測，因為壓力訊號與溶質前緣屬於不同的物理過程。","textEn":"Unsynchronized clocks create artificial phase lag and distort inferred diffusivity. Even a strong pressure-cycle fit cannot replace salinity monitoring, because hydraulic signals and solute fronts describe different physical processes and require distinct supporting observations.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]},{"id":"b298-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「潮汐水頭衰減與相位延遲」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tidal-head attenuation and phase lag\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","不同儀器時鐘未同步，會產生假的相位延遲，進而扭曲推估的擴散率。","任何海岸含水層只要水位高出海面一公尺，實際鹽水界面就必定精確位於四十公尺深。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Unsynchronized clocks create artificial phase lag and distort inferred diffusivity.","Every coastal aquifer with one metre of freshwater head has an actual interface exactly forty metres deep."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同儀器時鐘未同步，會產生假的相位延遲，進而扭曲推估的擴散率。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unsynchronized clocks create artificial phase lag and distort inferred diffusivity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-fresh-salt-relations","v15s-itrc-la-barriers-case","v15s-ocwd-barrier-history","v15s-usgs-seawat4"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
